{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_012tFdcMrRjJwgnoffsvDMcx","type":"tool_result","content":"586 lines D rows 423 R rows 123\n# ERRORS.md — the error surface of libpng (C ground truth)\n\nEvery row is a **distinct rejection site** found by mechanically scanning\n`c_src/src/*.c`.  Two independent scans were merged:\n\n* **Part 1 — diagnostic rejections** (423 rows): every call to one of\n  `png_error`, `png_chunk_error`, `png_fixed_error`, `png_app_error`,\n  `png_app_warning`, `png_benign_error`, `png_chunk_benign_error`,\n  `png_warning`, `png_chunk_warning`.  These are observable at the FFI\n  boundary through the `error_fn` / `warning_fn` callbacks installed with\n  `png_set_error_fn`, so the differential harness can compare the *exact*\n  message text and the fatal/non-fatal outcome.\n* **Part 2 — silent sentinel-return rejections** (123 rows): every guarded\n  `return 0 / NULL / -1` in `c_src/src/*.c`.  These are observable through the\n  return value.\n\n`libpng` has **no `assert()`** (`grep -c \"assert\" c_src/src/*.c` == 0 for real\nasserts; `PNG_ABORT()` is reached only from `png_error` when no `jmp_buf` and no\n`error_fn` is installed — covered by row D-0 below).\n\n## How a row is checked off\n\n`tests/errors.rs` drives BOTH shared libraries through the same input and\nrecords, in order, every `(warning|error, message)` the library reports plus the\nreturn value / final state, then asserts the two traces are byte-identical.\nA row is checked off when the harness has actually **observed that site firing\nin both libraries with an identical trace**.  The observed-message set is dumped\nby the test and diffed against this table (see `tests/errors.rs`,\n`ERROR_SITE_COVERAGE`), so the check marks are machine-verified, not asserted by\nhand.\n\n## Part 1 — diagnostic rejections\n\n| # | function (file:line) | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | seen |\n|---|----------------------|---------