Every row is a **distinct rejection site** found by mechanically scanning\n`c_src/src/*.c`.  Two independent scans were merged:\n\n* **Part 1 — diagnostic rejections** (423 rows): every call to one of\n  `png_error`, `png_chunk_error`, `png_fixed_error`, `png_app_error`,\n  `png_app_warning`, `png_benign_error`, `png_chunk_benign_error`,\n  `png_warning`, `png_chunk_warning`.  These are observable at the FFI\n  boundary through the `error_fn` / `warning_fn` callbacks installed with\n  `png_set_error_fn`, so the differential harness can compare the *exact*\n  message text and the fatal/non-fatal outcome.\n* **Part 2 — silent sentinel-return rejections** (123 rows): every guarded\n  `return 0 / NULL / -1` in `c_src/src/*.c`.  These are observable through the\n  return value.\n\n`libpng` has **no `assert()`** (`grep -c \"assert\" c_src/src/*.c` == 0 for real\nasserts; `PNG_ABORT()` is reached only from `png_error` when no `jmp_buf` and no\n`error_fn` is installed — covered by row D-0 below).\n\n## How a row is checked off\n\n`tests/errors.rs` drives BOTH shared libraries through the same input and\nrecords, in order, every `(warning|error, message)` the library reports plus the\nreturn value / final state, then asserts the two traces are byte-identical.\nA row is checked off when the harness has actually **observed that site firing\nin both libraries with an identical trace**.  The observed-message set is dumped\nby the test and diffed against this table (see `tests/errors.rs`,\n`ERROR_SITE_COVERAGE`), so the check marks are machine-verified, not asserted by\nhand.\n\n## Part 1 — diagnostic rejections\n\n| # | function (file:line) | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | seen |\n|---|----------------------|---------------------------------------------|-------------------|------|\n| D-1 | `png_set_sig_bytes` (png.c:66) | `if (nb > 8) <- if (num_bytes < 0)  →  message: \"Too many bytes for PNG signature\"` | fatal: warning_fn/error_fn -> png_longjmp (never returns); operation aborted | [ ] |\n| D-2 | `PNG_FUNCTION` (png.c:120) | `if (size != 0 && items >= (~(png_alloc_size_t)0) / size) <- if (png_ptr == NULL)  →  message: \"Potential overflow in png_zalloc()\"` | non-fatal: warning_fn(\"<msg>\"), caller continues | [ ] |\n| D-3 | `png_user_version_check` (png.c:245) | `if ((png_ptr->flags & PNG_FLAG_LIBRARY_MISMATCH) != 0) <- if (user_png_ver != NULL)` | non-fatal: warning_fn(\"<msg>\"), caller continues | [ ] |\n| D-4 | `png_data_freer` (png.c:479) | `else if (freer == PNG_USER_WILL_FREE_DATA) <- if (freer == PNG_DESTROY_WILL_FREE_DATA)  →  message: \"Unknown freer parameter in png_data_freer\"` | fatal: warning_fn/error_fn -> png_longjmp (never returns); operation aborted | [ ] |\n| D-5 | `png_convert_to_rfc1123` (png.c:802) | `if (png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer(png_ptr->time_buffer, ptime) == 0) <- if (png_ptr != NULL)  →  message: \"Ignoring invalid time value\"` | non-fatal: warning_fn(\"<msg>\"), caller continues | [ ] |\n| D-6 | `png_icc_profile_error` (png.c:1571) | `if (is_ICC_signature(value) != 0)` | PNG_FLAG_BENIGN_ERRORS_WARN -> png_chunk_warning, else png_chunk_error (fatal) | [ ] |\n| D-7 | `png_set_rgb_coefficients` (png.c:1938) | `if (r+g+b != 32768) <- if (add != 0)  →  message: \"internal error handling cHRM coefficients\"` | fatal: warning_fn/error_fn -> png_longjmp (never returns); operation aborted | [ ] |\n| D-8 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:1971) | `if (width == 0)  →  message: \"Image width is zero in IHDR\"` | non-fatal: warning_fn(\"<msg>\"), caller continues | [ ] |\n| D-9 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:1977) | `if (width > PNG_UINT_31_MAX) <- if (width == 0)  →  message: \"Invalid image width in IHDR\"` | non-fatal: warning_fn(\"<msg>\"), caller continues | [ ] |\n| D-10 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:2007) | `if (((width + 7) & ~(png_alloc_size_t)7) > (((PNG_SIZE_MAX - 48 - 1) / 8) - 1)) <- if (width > PNG_UINT_31_MAX)  →  message: \"Image width is too large for this architecture\"` | non-fatal: warning_fn(\"<msg>\"), caller continues | [ ] |\n| D-11 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:2017) | `if (width > PNG_USER_WIDTH_MAX) <- if (width > png_ptr->user_width_max)  →  message: \"Image width exceeds user limit in IHDR\"` | non-fatal: warning_fn(\"<msg>\"), caller continues | [ ] |\n| D-12 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:2023) | `if (height == 0) <- if (width > PNG_USER_WIDTH_MAX)  →  message: \"Image height is zero in IHDR\"` | non-fatal: warning_fn(\"<msg>\"), caller continues | [ ] |\n| D-13 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:2029) | `if (height > PNG_UINT_31_MAX) <- if (height == 0)  →  message: \"Invalid image height in IHDR\"` | non-fatal: warning_fn(\"<msg>\"), caller continues | [ ] |\n| D-14 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:2039) | `if (height > PNG_USER_HEIGHT_MAX) <- if (height > png_ptr->user_height_max)  →  message: \"Image height exceeds user limit in IHDR\"` | non-fatal: warning_fn(\"<msg>\"), caller continues | [ ] |\n| D-15 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:2047) | `if (bit_depth != 1 && bit_depth != 2 && bit_depth != 4 && bit_depth != 8 && bit_depth != 16) <- if (height > PNG_USER_HEIGHT_MAX)  →  message: \"Invalid bit depth in IHDR\"` | non-fatal: warning_fn(\"<msg>\"), caller continues | [ ] |\n| D-16 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:2054) | `if (color_type < 0 \\|\\| color_type == 1 \\|\\| color_type == 5 \\|\\| color_type > 6) <- if (bit_depth != 1 && bit_depth != 2 && bit_depth != 4 && bit_depth != 8 && bit_depth != 16)  →  message: \"Invalid color type in IHDR\"` | non-fatal: warning_fn(\"<msg>\"), caller continues | [ ] |\n| D-17 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:2063) | `if (((color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE) && bit_depth > 8) \\|\\| ((color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_RGB \\|\\| color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_GRAY_ALPHA \\|\\| color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_RGB_ALPHA) && bit_depth < 8)) <- if (color_type < 0 \\|\\| color_type == 1 \\|\\| color_type == 5 \\|\\| color_type > 6)  →  message: \"Invalid color type/bit depth combination in IHDR\"` | non-fatal: warning_fn(\"<msg>\"), caller