{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_vi2jvrovxzvjpq2djo6py66e7lhbiaklspqa6oomamlo7xbslrvq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01Y739NwgyFJ1qevUnnJG3f5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-CVzjKq/translated_rust/tests/common/shim.c","content":"/* Differential-test support shim.\n *\n * libpng reports fatal errors by calling png_longjmp(), which calls the\n * application-supplied longjmp_fn on the jmp_buf returned by\n * png_set_longjmp_fn().  A Rust test cannot host the setjmp() itself (setjmp\n * has no sound Rust binding), so this tiny C object provides the setjmp frame\n * and the body of the operation is a Rust callback.\n *\n * This is *test scaffolding only*: it is compiled into its own shared object,\n * dlopen'd by the test, and is never linked into either libpng under test.\n * Nothing in c_src/ is modified or used.\n */\n#include <setjmp.h>\n#include <stddef.h>\n\n/* png_longjmp() does `png_ptr->longjmp_fn(*png_ptr->jmp_buf_ptr, val)`, i.e. it\n * passes the decayed jmp_buf; the type therefore matches `longjmp` exactly,\n * which is what png.h's own png_jmpbuf() macro relies on. */\ntypedef void (*png_longjmp_ptr_t)(jmp_buf, int);\ntypedef jmp_buf *(*set_longjmp_fn_t)(void *png_ptr, png_longjmp_ptr_t fn,\n                                     size_t jmp_buf_size);\n\n/* Run `body(arg)` with a libpng error trap armed on `png_ptr`.\n *\n * returns 0  -> body ran to completion\n *         1  -> libpng raised a fatal error (png_error/png_longjmp)\n *        -1  -> png_set_longjmp_fn() returned NULL (ABI/OOM failure)\n */\nint harness_run(set_longjmp_fn_t set_longjmp_fn, void *png_ptr,\n                void (*body)(void *), void *arg)\n{\n   jmp_buf *jb = set_longjmp_fn(png_ptr, longjmp, sizeof(jmp_buf));\n\n   if (jb == NULL)\n      return -1;\n\n   if (setjmp(*jb) != 0)\n      return 1;\n\n   body(arg);\n   return 0;\n}\n\n/* Same, but the body may also be entered when no png_ptr exists yet (the\n * create call itself).  `out` receives the png_ptr the body produced. */\nsize_t harness_jmp_buf_size(void)\n{\n   return sizeof(jmp_buf);\n}\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10328,"cache_read_input_tokens":118508,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":10328,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"309de29f-cb7a-4138-9016-7ab2e7ef6079","uuid":"66826d39-dc33-4721-84bd-705fcba7bbf6","timestamp":"2026-08-23T02:03:11.620Z"}
