{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_dvsxae7eqyit63ggxzntl6hxbbg3bazkbvnfwyfma2f6yifaqqoq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01Fjv9Nnhfo3chVZxRpuENA4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-CVzjKq/translated_rust/tests/HARNESS.md","content":"# Differential test harness — how to write a test\n\nRead this before adding a test file.  `tests/write_read.rs` is the canonical\nexample; `tests/smoke.rs` is the smallest one.\n\n## Ground rules\n\n* The **C code in `c_src/` is the ground truth and must never be modified.**\n  If C and Rust disagree, the Rust translation in `src/` is wrong.\n* Never call a Rust function directly.  Everything goes through\n  `common::Api`, whose fields are function pointers resolved with\n  `libloading` from the two `.so`s.  This exercises the `#[no_mangle]`\n  wrappers.\n* Build and run with `./check.sh --test <name>` (it rebuilds the C `.so`, the\n  Rust cdylib and the setjmp shim first — plain `cargo test` may silently test\n  a stale `.so`).\n\n## Skeleton\n\n```rust\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\n\n#[test]\nfn my_case() {\n    assert_same(\"human readable case name\", |api| unsafe {\n        let mut o = Outcome::default();\n        let (png, info) = new_write(api);           // or new_read(api)\n        (api.png_set_write_fn)(png, core::ptr::null_mut(),\n                               Some(write_cb), Some(flush_cb));\n        let g = guarded(api, png, &mut || {\n            // ... drive libpng here; png_error() longjmps back out of\n            //     `guarded`, which returns Guard::Error(msg)\n            (api.png_set_IHDR)(png, info, 4, 4, 8, PNG_COLOR_TYPE_RGB,\n                               PNG_INTERLACE_NONE, PNG_COMPRESSION_TYPE_BASE,\n                               PNG_FILTER_TYPE_BASE);\n            (api.png_write_info)(png, info);\n            (api.png_write_end)(png, info);\n        });\n        o.push(format!(\"guard={:?}\", g));            // record the outcome\n        o.output = std::mem::take(&mut tls().output); // and the bytes written\n        destroy_write(api, png, info);\n        o\n    });\n}\n```\n\n`assert_same` runs the closure **twice** — once with the C `Api`, once with the\nRust `Api`, each with a fresh `Tls` — and asserts that\n\n1. the ordered event trace is identical, and\n2. `Outcome::output` is byte-identical.\n\nIt panics with a readable diff of the first difference.  It also fails if a\nscenario recorded *nothing* (which would mean the test does not exercise\nanything).\n\n## What to record\n\nAnything the library tells you.  Cheap and effective:\n\n* `log(\"...\")` — appends to the trace from anywhere, including from a callback.\n  Prefer `log` over `o.push` when ordering relative to callbacks matters.\n* `o.push(\"...\")` — appended after all callback events.\n* `o.output` — the bytes to compare (written file, decoded rows, …).\n* Return values, out-parameters, `png_get_*` results, `Guard`, warning text.\n\n**Record aggressively.** A value you do not record cannot diverge visibly.\n\n## Available pieces (`tests/common/`)\n\n| item | what it is |\n|------|-----------|\n| `libs()` | `&'static Libs { c: Api, rust: Api, shim: Shim }` |\n| `Api` | one field per exported symbol — **all 384** of them, generated by `tools/gen_api.py` from `png.h` + `pngpriv.h`.  `grep '<name>' tests/common/api.rs` to see a signature. |\n| `guarded(api, png, &mut || {...}) -> Guard` | arms libpng's error trap; `Guard::Ok` / `Guard::Error(String)` / `Guard::NoTrap` |\n| `new_read` / `new_write` / `destroy_read` / `destroy_write` | create/destroy with the harness error+warning handlers installed |\n| `read_cb` / `write_cb` / `flush_cb` | memory IO callbacks; input in `tls().input`, output in `tls().output` |\n| `read_status_cb` / `write_status_cb` | row/pass callbacks that log |\n| `user_transform_cb` | a deterministic user transform that logs and mangles the row |\n| `malloc_cb` / `free_cb` | a logging allocator for `png_set_mem_fn` |\n| `tls()` | per-thread `Tls { trace, input, in_pos, output, flushes, rows, counter, allocs, .. }` |\n| `Rng::new(seed)` | SplitMix64: `u32() u8() below(n) range(lo,hi) bytes(n) pick(&[..]) bool()` |\n| `Img::random(rng, w, h, ct, bd)` | a random image of a legal shape (+ palette) |\n| `write_image` / `write_plain` / `WriteOpts` | drive a whole write; `extra` hook runs between `png_set_IHDR` and `png_write_info` |\n| `read_image` / `read_plain` / `ReadOpts` / `RowMode` | drive a whole read; `setup` hook runs right after `png_read_info` |\n| `log_info(api, png, info, tag)` | dump the whole IHDR/rowbytes/valid state |\n| `chunk(name, data)` / `chunk_bad_crc` / `insert_before` / `insert_after_last` / `split_chunks` / `crc32` / `SIG` | build or patch a PNG datastream by hand |\n| `VALID_SHAPES` | the 15 legal `(color_type, bit_depth)` pairs |\n| `PNG_*` constants | in `common::types` |\n\n## Gotchas\n\n* `png_error` never returns — it `longjmp`s out of `guarded`.  Anything after\n  the failing call inside the `guarded` body is skipped, in **both** libraries,\n  which is exactly what we want to compare.\n* After `Guard::Error` the `png_struct` may only be destroyed.\n* Keep buffers alive across the call (`let v = ...; (api.f)(v.as_ptr())`) —\n  a temporary would dangle.\n* `png_read_row` needs `rowbytes` **after** `png_read_update_info`, which can\n  grow the row (expand, gray→rgb, filler, …).\n* Seed every `Rng` from a constant so failures reproduce.\n* Use many randomised inputs per configuration — one hand-picked value per\n  configuration is not enough.\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3453,"cache_read_input_tokens":223422,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3453,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"309de29f-cb7a-4138-9016-7ab2e7ef6079","uuid":"d00f8018-dbfd-4184-a185-af8a8b843fa7","timestamp":"2026-08-23T02:16:54.941Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Fjv9Nnhfo3chVZxRpuENA4","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-CVzjKq/translated_rust/tests/HARNESS.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"309de29f-cb7a-4138-9016-7ab2e7ef6079","uuid":"a5932a12-c5d6-4077-8fad-50933c36aaf6","timestamp":"2026-08-23T02:16:54.950Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-CVzjKq/translated_rust/tests/HARNESS.md","content":"# Differential test harness — how to write a test\n\nRead this before adding a test file.  `tests/write_read.rs` is the canonical\nexample; `tests/smoke.rs` is the smallest one.\n\n## Ground rules\n\n* The **C code in `c_src/` is the ground truth and must never be modified.**\n  If C and Rust disagree, the Rust translation in `src/` is wrong.\n* Never call a Rust function directly.  Everything goes through\n  `common::Api`, whose fields are function pointers resolved with\n  `libloading` from the two `.so`s.  This exercises the `#[no_mangle]`\n  wrappers.\n* Build and run with `./check.sh --test <name>` (it rebuilds the C `.so`, the\n  Rust cdylib and the setjmp shim first — plain `cargo test` may silently test\n  a stale `.so`).\n\n## Skeleton\n\n```rust\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\n\n#[test]\nfn my_case() {\n    assert_same(\"human readable case name\", |api| unsafe {\n        let mut o = Outcome::default();\n        let (png, info) = new_write(api);           // or new_read(api)\n        (api.png_set_write_fn)(png, core::ptr::null_mut(),\n                               Some(write_cb), Some(flush_cb));\n        let g = guarded(api, png, &mut || {\n            // ... drive libpng here; png_error() longjmps back out of\n            //     `guarded`, which returns Guard::Error(msg)\n            (api.png_set_IHDR)(png, info, 4, 4, 8, PNG_COLOR_TYPE_RGB,\n                               PNG_INTERLACE_NONE, PNG_COMPRESSION_TYPE_BASE,\n                               PNG_FILTER_TYPE_BASE);\n            (api.png_write_info)(png, info);\n            (api.png_write_end)(png, info);\n        });\n        o.push(format!(\"guard={:?}\", g));            // record the outcome\n        o.output = std::mem::take(&mut tls().output); // and the bytes written\n        destroy_write(api, png, info);\n        o\n    });\n}\n```\n\n`assert_same` runs the closure **twice** — once with the C `Api`, once with the\nRust `Api`, each with a fresh `Tls` — and asserts that\n\n1. the ordered event trace is identical, and\n2. `Outcome::output` is byte-identical.\n\nIt panics with a readable diff of the first difference.  It also fails if a\nscenario recorded *nothing* (which would mean the test does not exercise\nanything).\n\n## What to record\n\nAnything the library tells you.  Cheap and effective:\n\n* `log(\"...\")` — appends to the trace from anywhere, including from a callback.\n  Prefer `log` over `o.push` when ordering relative to callbacks matters.\n* `o.push(\"...\")` — appended after all callback events.\n* `o.output` — the bytes to compare (written file, decoded rows, …).\n* Return values, out-parameters, `png_get_*` results, `Guard`, warning text.\n\n**Record aggressively.** A value you do not record cannot diverge visibly.\n\n## Available pieces (`tests/common/`)\n\n| item | what it is |\n|------|-----------|\n| `libs()` | `&'static Libs { c: Api, rust: Api, shim: Shim }` |\n| `Api` | one field per exported symbol — **all 384** of them, generated by `tools/gen_api.py` from `png.h` + `pngpriv.h`.  `grep '<name>' tests/common/api.rs` to see a signature. |\n| `guarded(api, png, &mut || {...}) -> Guard` | arms libpng's error trap; `Guard::Ok` / `Guard::Error(String)` / `Guard::NoTrap` |\n| `new_read` / `new_write` / `destroy_read` / `destroy_write` | create/destroy with the harness error+warning handlers installed |\n| `read_cb` / `write_cb` / `flush_cb` | memory IO callbacks; input in `tls().input`, output in `tls().output` |\n| `read_status_cb` / `write_status_cb` | row/pass callbacks that log |\n| `user_transform_cb` | a deterministic user transform that logs and mangles the row |\n| `malloc_cb` / `free_cb` | a logging allocator for `png_set_mem_fn` |\n| `tls()` | per-thread `Tls { trace, input, in_pos, output, flushes, rows, counter, allocs, .. }` |\n| `Rng::new(seed)` | SplitMix64: `u32() u8() below(n) range(lo,hi) bytes(n) pick(&[..]) bool()` |\n| `Img::random(rng, w, h, ct, bd)` | a random image of a legal shape (+ palette) |\n| `write_image` / `write_plain` / `WriteOpts` | drive a whole write; `extra` hook runs between `png_set_IHDR` and `png_write_info` |\n| `read_image` / `read_plain` / `ReadOpts` / `RowMode` | drive a whole read; `setup` hook runs right after `png_read_info` |\n| `log_info(api, png, info, tag)` | dump the whole IHDR/rowbytes/valid state |\n| `chunk(name, data)` / `chunk_bad_crc` / `insert_before` / `insert_after_last` / `split_chunks` / `crc32` / `SIG` | build or patch a PNG datastream by hand |\n| `VALID_SHAPES` | the 15 legal `(color_type, bit_depth)` pairs |\n| `PNG_*` constants | in `common::types` |\n\n## Gotchas\n\n* `png_error` never returns — it `longjmp`s out of `guarded`.  Anything after\n  the failing call inside the `guarded` body is skipped, in **both** libraries,\n  which is exactly what we want to compare.\n* After `Guard::Error` the `png_struct` may only be destroyed.\n* Keep buffers alive across the call (`let v = ...; (api.f)(v.as_ptr())`) —\n  a temporary would dangle.\n* `png_read_row` needs `rowbytes` **after** `png_read_update_info`, which can\n  grow the row (expand, gray→rgb, filler, …).\n* Seed every `Rng` from a constant so failures reproduce.\n* Use many randomised inputs per configuration — one hand-picked value per\n  configuration is not enough.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
