_write_end with info NULL` | chunks emitted before PLTE vs after; png_write_end(png, NULL) | [ ] |\n209:| C-154 | `png_read_info, png_read_end with info NULL, png_read_update_info` | png_read_end(png, NULL) and with an info struct; unread rows at png_read_end | [ ] |\n215:| C-1 | `lowlevel::byte_accessors` |\n216:| C-2 | `lowlevel::sig_cmp` |\n217:| C-3 | `lowlevel::muldiv` |\n218:| C-4 | `lowlevel::reciprocal` |\n219:| C-5 | `lowlevel::fixed` |\n220:| C-6 | `lowlevel::gamma_scalar` |\n221:| C-7 | `transforms::gamma_tables` |\n222:| C-8 | `lowlevel::xyz_xy` |\n223:| C-9 | `lowlevel::fp_parse` |\n224:| C-10 | `lowlevel::ascii_from` |\n225:| C-11 | `lowlevel::safecat_format` |\n226:| C-12 | `lowlevel::crc` |\n227:| C-13 | `lowlevel::row_ops` |\n228:| C-14 | `lowlevel::read_filter_row` |\n229:| C-15 | `lowlevel::write_find_filter` |\n230:| C-16 | `lowlevel::combine_row` |\n231:| C-17 | `lowlevel::interlace_row` |\n232:| C-18 | `lowlevel::check_ihdr` |\n233:| C-19 | `lowlevel::check_keyword` |\n234:| C-20 | `lowlevel::zstream_error` |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01ReZusWgDJG9J6x9tJWUP9p","session_id":"309de29f-cb7a-4138-9016-7ab2e7ef6079","uuid":"0083c795-057d-4528-a361-ebf1a36e536a","timestamp":"2026-08-23T02:17:56.080Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write lowlevel differential tests"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_x2aymq36pwfa3qkxzqyu6nwhmqhfwg66tofxedrgfmexm2qxkauq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01BMWL9AwQNN8BAN8oW4HXMy","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write chunks differential tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"You are working in `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-CVzjKq/translated_rust` (cd there for everything).\n\nThis project is a C-to-Rust translation of libpng. `c_src/` holds the ORIGINAL C (ground truth, NEVER modify anything under `c_src/`). `src/` holds the Rust translation. A differential test harness already exists that dlopens BOTH shared libraries and compares them.\n\n## Read first (mandatory)\n1. `tests/HARNESS.md` — how to write a test with this harness.\n2. `tests/common/mod.rs`, `tests/common/helpers.rs`, `tests/common/types.rs` — the harness.\n3. `tests/write_read.rs` — the canonical example. Match its style.\n4. `tests/common/api.rs` is GENERATED (do not edit) — grep it for the exact Rust signature of any libpng symbol, e.g. `grep -n 'png_set_pCAL' tests/common/api.rs`.\n5. `CONFIGS.md` — your rows are the \"chunks::*\" rows in the \"Row → test mapping\" table (C-105 … C-129 area, plus `chunks::iccp` C-21, `chunks::text_compression`, `chunks::set_invalid`, `chunks::user_chunk_fn`, `chunks::write_order`).\n\n## Your task\nCreate **`tests/chunks.rs`** with these `#[test]` functions (names must match the\nCONFIGS.md \"Row → test mapping\" column):\n\n- `round_trip` — ONE test that loops over ALL 21 ancillary chunk types listed in\n  CONFIGS.md (gAMA cHRM sRGB iCCP sBIT bKGD hIST tRNS pHYs oFFs tIME pCAL sCAL\n  sPLT tEXt zTXt iTXt eXIf cICP cLLI mDCV). For each chunk: set it with the\n  `png_set_*` API on the write side (using randomised values from the CONFIGS row\n  description, MANY iterations with a fixed-seed `Rng`), write a small image,\n  compare the produced file bytes; then read the file back with both libraries and\n  compare everything `png_get_*` returns for that chunk (all out-parameters,\n  strings, lengths, and the `png_get_valid` mask). Also cover: chunk absent, chunk\n  present once, chunk present twice in the datastream (use `insert_before` /\n  `insert_after_last` from helpers to duplicate the raw chunk).\n  Feel free to split this into several `#[test]` fns (`round_trip`,\n  `round_trip_2`, ...) if it gets long, but cover every chunk.\n- `iccp` (C-21) — png_set_iCCP/png_get_iCCP plus the ICC validation paths\n  (`png_icc_check_header`, `png_icc_check_length`, `png_icc_check_tag_table` in\n  `c_src/src/png.c`): build synthetic ICC profiles (correct sRGB-like profile,\n  wrong length field, bad signature, bad tag table, 0 tags, huge tag count) and\n  feed them through an iCCP chunk on the READ side; also test\n  `png_set_option(png, PNG_SKIP_sRGB_CHECK_PROFILE, ON/OFF)`. Compare all\n  warnings/errors verbatim.\n- `text_compression` — png_set_text_compression_level/strategy/mem_level/\n  window_bits/method over their full ranges, observed through a compressed\n  zTXt/iTXt/iCCP payload.\n- `unknown` — png_set_unknown_chunks / png_get_unknown_chunks /\n  png_set_unknown_chunk_location / png_set_keep_unknown_chunks /\n  png_handle_as_unknown / png_chunk_unknown_handling: the full cross product in\n  the CONFIGS row (keep AS_DEFAULT/NEVER/IF_SAFE/ALWAYS × chunk list NULL vs\n  named × chunk name critical/ancillary/private/reserved/safe-to-copy × location\n  × data size 0..1024).\n- `rows_and_freer` — png_set_rows / png_get_rows / png_free_data / png_data_freer\n  with every `PNG_FREE_*` mask.\n- `text_many` — png_set_text / png_set_text_2 with num_text 0, 1, many (> 8 to hit\n  the realloc path), compression values -3..2.\n- `set_invalid` — png_set_invalid / png_get_valid for every `PNG_INFO_*` bit.\n- `user_chunk_fn` — png_set_read_user_chunk_fn / png_get_user_chunk_ptr with the\n  callback returning -1, 0 and 1, on ancillary and critical unknown chunks.\n- `write_order` — png_write_info_before_PLTE vs png_write_info, and\n  `png_write_end(png, NULL)`.\n\n## Method\nFor each chunk, FIRST read the C setter in `c_src/src/pngset.c`, the C writer in\n`c_src/src/pngwutil.c` and the C reader in `c_src/src/pngrutil.c`, so you know\nexactly which values are accepted, what is stored, and what is emitted. Then drive\nboth libraries and compare. Record aggressively — every out-parameter, every\nreturned string (as bytes), every length, every warning message.\n\nCareful with lifetimes: `png_set_iCCP`, `png_set_text`, `png_set_sPLT`,\n`png_set_pCAL`, `png_set_unknown_chunks` etc. take pointers to caller memory;\nkeep the `CString`s / `Vec`s alive until after `png_write_info` (bind them to\n`let` variables in the enclosing scope, not temporaries).\n\n## Iterate to green\nRun `timeout 600 ./check.sh --test chunks 2>&1 | tail -40` and fix until green.\n\nIf C and Rust DIVERGE:\n1. First rule out a bug in your test (dangling pointer, wrong struct layout, wrong\n   buffer size, reading uninitialised out-params the C never writes).\n2. Then read the C source and fix the RUST translation in `src/` with small\n   surgical `Edit` calls. Never touch `c_src/`.\n3. Note every divergence you fixed.\n\n## Report back\n- the list of `#[test]` fns and the CONFIGS rows each covers\n- `wc -l tests/chunks.rs`\n- the final `cargo test` result line\n- EVERY divergence found, with C source location, wrong Rust code, and the fix"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2419,"cache_read_input_tokens":226875,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2419,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"309de29f-cb7a-4138-9016-7ab2e7ef6079","uuid":"7de07a93-3b93-44c8-82e9-6e463e374b92","timestamp":"2026-08-23T02:17:56.515Z"}
