`src/` was needed; `c_src/` untouched.\n\nBecause a clean first pass is not evidence of a good test, I mutation-tested it: five deliberate one-line breakages in `src/gen/` (`png_do_invert` loop bound, `png_calculate_crc` result, `png_combine_row`'s `pass < 6`, `png_write_find_filter`'s 128 threshold, `png_do_check_palette_indexes`' 8-bit branch) were each caught by the intended test, then reverted and verified gone. So the four rows whose target is only reachable through a public path really do reach it.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n- **`png_muldiv_warn` does not exist** in this libpng — no definition anywhere in `c_src/`, not an exported symbol, not in `tests/common/api.rs`. Row C-3 covers `png_muldiv` only; there's a comment saying so.\n- **Row numbering**: the task listed `time_conv` as C-25, but `CONFIGS.md`'s own mapping table puts `lowlevel::time_conv` at **C-24** and `smoke::version_numbers_match` at C-25. I followed the mapping table; the skipped rows are therefore C-7, C-21, C-23.\n- Four functions cannot be called with caller-supplied state and are driven through the public path (each with a comment naming the row): `png_write_find_filter` (writes into the IDAT stream) via full writes with all 32 filter masks; `png_combine_row` via interlaced `png_read_row` with a non-NULL `display_row` and pre-filled destinations; `png_do_check_palette_indexes` (walks `png_ptr->row_buf`) via palette writes/reads plus `png_get_palette_max`; `png_reset_crc`/`png_calculate_crc` via a custom read callback that recomputes the CRC at the exact instant `png_crc_error` has read the 4 CRC bytes, so a wrong CRC becomes an observable \"CRC error\".\n- `png_zstream_error` writes only `zstream.msg`, which is unreadable externally. Direct calls cover every `ret` in −8..4; the message text is compared through the two paths that report it verbatim — an invalid deflate parameter (`png_deflate_claim` → `png_error(png_ptr->zstream.msg)`) and damaged/truncated zTXt streams on the read side.\n- Deliberately excluded, with comments: pixel depths outside `{1,2,4,8,16,24,32,48,64}` (`png_read_filter_row_avg` underflows `rowbytes - bpp` inside libpng itself), and negative gammas for `png_gamma_*_correct` (the C `double`→integer cast is UB there, so C has no defined behaviour to match)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":439,"cache_read_input_tokens":262636,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":439,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01ReZusWgDJG9J6x9tJWUP9p","session_id":"309de29f-cb7a-4138-9016-7ab2e7ef6079","uuid":"839286f8-4377-4e28-8171-c7a9abd9f12b","timestamp":"2026-08-23T02:41:40.462Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write lowlevel differential tests"}
