{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_lglkz5i3wqykdwng7oin3o4hmqfpqecrokraedr3ngr57vpo6otq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01TGCoGUz85WiUHtvgs8whHb","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write progressive read tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"You are working in `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-CVzjKq/translated_rust` (cd there for everything).\n\nlibpng C-to-Rust translation. `c_src/` = ORIGINAL C, ground truth, **NEVER modify anything under `c_src/`**. `src/` = the Rust translation. A differential harness already dlopens BOTH `.so`s and compares them.\n\n## Read first (mandatory)\n1. `tests/HARNESS.md`\n2. `tests/common/mod.rs`, `tests/common/helpers.rs`, `tests/common/forked.rs`, `tests/common/types.rs`\n3. `tests/write_read.rs` and `tests/transforms.rs` — canonical examples, match their style\n4. `tests/common/api.rs` is GENERATED (never edit) — grep it for exact signatures\n5. `CONFIGS.md` — your rows are the `progressive::*` ones: `progressive::chunk_sizes`,\n   `progressive::pause_skip`, `progressive::split_boundaries`, `progressive::transforms`\n6. The C: `c_src/src/pngpread.c` in full, plus `png_set_progressive_read_fn` and\n   `png_progressive_combine_row` (`pngread.c`/`pngpread.c`).\n\n## Your task\nCreate **`tests/progressive.rs`** with `#[test]` fns named exactly\n`chunk_sizes`, `pause_skip`, `split_boundaries`, `transforms`.\n\nThe progressive reader is driven like this: `png_set_progressive_read_fn(png,\nprogressive_ptr, info_callback, row_callback, end_callback)` then\n`png_process_data(png, info, buf, len)` repeatedly. The callbacks must be Rust\n`extern \"C\"` fns that record everything into the harness's `tls()` (see how\n`read_status_cb` / `user_transform_cb` do it in `tests/common/`). In the row\ncallback, call `png_progressive_combine_row` into a destination row you keep in\n`tls().rows`, and log the row number, pass and the resulting bytes.\n\n- `chunk_sizes`: for every one of the 15 `VALID_SHAPES` × interlace NONE/ADAM7,\n  build a file with the C library (see `write_plain` / `write_image` in\n  `tests/common/helpers.rs`) and then feed it to BOTH libraries in fixed-size\n  pieces of 1, 2, 3, 5, 13, 100, 1024, 8192 bytes and all at once. Compare the\n  full event trace and every decoded row byte. Use several randomised image\n  contents and sizes per shape (fixed seed).\n- `split_boundaries`: adversarial feeding — zero-length `png_process_data` calls,\n  chunk headers split across feeds at every possible offset, IDAT split mid-row,\n  feeding the 8-byte signature one byte at a time, feeding more data after IEND,\n  and truncated input (feed only the first N bytes and stop, for many N). Also\n  exercise `png_set_sig_bytes` + `png_process_data` with a pre-consumed signature.\n- `pause_skip`: `png_process_data_pause(png, save)` with save = 0 and 1, called\n  after every feed, resuming until the file is consumed; and\n  `png_process_data_skip(png)` — read `png_process_data_skip` and\n  `png_push_read_chunk` in `c_src/src/pngpread.c` to see what state makes the\n  skip meaningful (`png_ptr->process_mode == PNG_SKIP_MODE`), and construct that\n  state. Compare the return values of both functions on every call.\n- `transforms`: the progressive reader with read transforms installed in the\n  info callback (`png_set_expand`, `png_set_strip_16`, `png_set_gray_to_rgb`,\n  `png_set_palette_to_rgb`, `png_set_packing`, `png_set_bgr`, `png_set_swap`,\n  `png_set_filler`, `png_set_invert_mono`, `png_set_gamma`, plus random\n  combinations) — remember to call `png_read_update_info` in the info callback\n  and to size the destination rows from `png_get_rowbytes` afterwards.\n\nAlso cover the error paths of the progressive reader (they are ERRORS.md rows in\n`pngpread.c`): a bad signature, an unexpected chunk, IDAT before PLTE, a\ntoo-short IDAT, and `png_process_data` called after the end.\n\n## Rules\n- Record aggressively: every callback invocation, every row, every return value,\n  every warning. A value you do not record cannot diverge visibly.\n- Use `assert_same` for scenarios that cannot crash; use `assert_same_forked`\n  (from `tests/common/forked.rs`) for anything that might crash or abort — a\n  crash is then a *compared observation* rather than the end of the test run.\n- Fixed `Rng` seeds so failures reproduce.\n- Iterate: `timeout 600 ./check.sh --test progressive 2>&1 | tail -40` until green.\n- If C and Rust diverge: first rule out a bug in your own test (uninitialised\n  destination row — libpng's `big_row_buf` is `png_malloc`ed not zeroed, so\n  reading bytes past the real row data compares uninitialised heap; dangling\n  pointers; wrong rowbytes). Only then read the C and fix the RUST side in `src/`\n  with small surgical `Edit` calls. Never touch `c_src/`.\n- Do not edit anything in `tests/common/` — other agents are working there. If you\n  need a helper, put it in your own file.\n\n## Report back\n- the list of `#[test]` fns and the CONFIGS rows each covers\n- `wc -l tests/progressive.rs`\n- the number of differential comparisons performed (count them)\n- the final `cargo test` result line\n- EVERY divergence found, with C source location, the wrong Rust code, and the fix"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":370644,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":370644,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"309de29f-cb7a-4138-9016-7ab2e7ef6079","uuid":"e481db6e-4e59-4170-8a3f-7bd9afad69a6","timestamp":"2026-08-23T02:52:33.595Z"}
