{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_lglkz5i3wqykdwng7oin3o4hmqfpqecrokraedr3ngr57vpo6otq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01DkTVAznv6jg5QHC72BbbtR","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write simplified API tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"You are working in `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-CVzjKq/translated_rust` (cd there for everything).\n\nlibpng C-to-Rust translation. `c_src/` = ORIGINAL C, ground truth, **NEVER modify anything under `c_src/`**. `src/` = the Rust translation. A differential harness already dlopens BOTH `.so`s and compares them.\n\n## Read first (mandatory)\n1. `tests/HARNESS.md`\n2. `tests/common/mod.rs`, `tests/common/helpers.rs`, `tests/common/forked.rs`, `tests/common/types.rs`\n   (note `png_image` and all the `PNG_FORMAT_*` / `PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_*` constants are in `types.rs`)\n3. `tests/write_read.rs` — canonical example, match its style\n4. `tests/common/api.rs` is GENERATED (never edit) — grep it for exact signatures\n5. `CONFIGS.md` — your rows are the `simplified::*` ones: `simplified::read_formats`,\n   `simplified::read_stdio`, `simplified::write_formats`, `simplified::round_trip`\n6. The C: the whole simplified API at the end of `c_src/src/pngread.c`\n   (`png_image_begin_read_from_*`, `png_image_finish_read`, `png_image_free`,\n   `png_image_read_*`, `png_safe_execute`, `png_image_error`) and the end of\n   `c_src/src/pngwrite.c` (`png_image_write_to_memory/stdio/file`,\n   `png_image_write_*`). Also read the `PNG_IMAGE_*` macros in `c_src/include/png.h`\n   (`PNG_IMAGE_ROW_STRIDE`, `PNG_IMAGE_BUFFER_SIZE`, `PNG_IMAGE_SIZE`,\n   `PNG_IMAGE_COLORMAP_SIZE`, `PNG_IMAGE_PNG_SIZE_MAX`) — you must compute buffer\n   sizes exactly the way they do.\n\n## Your task\nCreate **`tests/simplified.rs`** with `#[test]` fns named exactly\n`read_formats`, `read_stdio`, `write_formats`, `round_trip`.\n\nThe simplified API never `longjmp`s out (it traps errors internally via\n`png_safe_execute` and reports through `image.warning_or_error` +\n`image.message`), so you normally do NOT need `guarded` — but you MUST compare\n`image.warning_or_error`, the whole 64-byte `image.message`, `image.width`,\n`image.height`, `image.format`, `image.flags`, `image.colormap_entries`, the\nreturn value of every call, AND every byte of the output buffer / colormap.\n\n- `read_formats` (C-137): build source PNGs with the C low-level writer for many\n  shapes (all 15 `VALID_SHAPES`, interlaced and not, with and without tRNS /\n  bKGD / gAMA / sRGB), then for each one call\n  `png_image_begin_read_from_memory` + `png_image_finish_read` on BOTH libraries\n  with `image.format` set to every output format: GRAY, GA, AG, RGB, BGR, RGBA,\n  ARGB, BGRA, ABGR, each plain and `|PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_COLORMAP`, plus\n  LINEAR_Y, LINEAR_Y_ALPHA, LINEAR_RGB, LINEAR_RGB_ALPHA; `image.flags` in\n  {0, PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_FAST, PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_16BIT_sRGB,\n   PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_COLORSPACE_NOT_sRGB}; `background` NULL and a random\n  `png_color` ; `row_stride` = 0 (means \"natural\"), the natural value, a larger\n  positive value, and the negative of each (bottom-up). Allocate the buffer with\n  `PNG_IMAGE_BUFFER_SIZE` semantics and initialise it to a known pattern so that\n  bytes libpng does NOT write are still compared.\n- `read_stdio` (C-138): the same through `png_image_begin_read_from_stdio` (a real\n  `FILE*` from `fopen`) and `png_image_begin_read_from_file` (a real path under\n  `target/`). Use `libc`-style `extern \"C\" { fn fopen(..); fn fclose(..); }`\n  declarations in your own file (there is no `libc` crate available offline).\n- `write_formats` (C-139): `png_image_write_to_memory` (both as a size query with\n  a NULL buffer and with a real buffer that is exactly big enough, one byte too\n  small, and much bigger), `png_image_write_to_stdio`, `png_image_write_to_file`,\n  over every input format × `convert_to_8bit` 0/1 × colormap present/absent ×\n  `row_stride` positive and negative. Compare the produced PNG bytes exactly.\n- `round_trip` (C-140): write with the simplified API, read back with the\n  simplified API, in every format; compare.\n\nAlso cover the simplified API's own error paths (ERRORS.md rows in pngread.c /\npngwrite.c): `image.version` wrong (0, 2, 0xffffffff), `image.opaque` non-NULL on\nentry, a format with undefined bits set, `width`/`height` 0 or huge,\n`colormap_entries` > 256, NULL `memory`, NULL `image`, a colormapped format with\na NULL colormap, `png_image_free` called twice, `png_image_finish_read` without a\npreceding begin.\n\n## Rules\n- Record aggressively; a value you do not record cannot diverge visibly.\n- Use `assert_same` normally; use `assert_same_forked` (from\n  `tests/common/forked.rs`) for anything that might crash. Prefer forked for the\n  NULL/garbage error cases.\n- Fixed `Rng` seeds.\n- Iterate: `timeout 600 ./check.sh --test simplified 2>&1 | tail -40` until green.\n- If C and Rust diverge: first rule out a bug in your own test (wrong buffer size\n  — recompute it exactly as `PNG_IMAGE_BUFFER_SIZE` does; comparing bytes libpng\n  never writes; a dangling `FILE*`). Only then read the C and fix the RUST side in\n  `src/` with small surgical `Edit` calls. Never touch `c_src/`.\n- Do not edit anything in `tests/common/` — other agents are working there.\n\n## Report back\n- the list of `#[test]` fns and the CONFIGS rows each covers\n- `wc -l tests/simplified.rs`\n- the number of differential comparisons performed (count them)\n- the final `cargo test` result line\n- EVERY divergence found, with C source location, the wrong Rust code, and the fix"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":370644,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":370644,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"conte