emory` + `png_image_finish_read` on BOTH libraries\n  with `image.format` set to every output format: GRAY, GA, AG, RGB, BGR, RGBA,\n  ARGB, BGRA, ABGR, each plain and `|PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_COLORMAP`, plus\n  LINEAR_Y, LINEAR_Y_ALPHA, LINEAR_RGB, LINEAR_RGB_ALPHA; `image.flags` in\n  {0, PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_FAST, PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_16BIT_sRGB,\n   PNG_IMAGE_FLAG_COLORSPACE_NOT_sRGB}; `background` NULL and a random\n  `png_color` ; `row_stride` = 0 (means \"natural\"), the natural value, a larger\n  positive value, and the negative of each (bottom-up). Allocate the buffer with\n  `PNG_IMAGE_BUFFER_SIZE` semantics and initialise it to a known pattern so that\n  bytes libpng does NOT write are still compared.\n- `read_stdio` (C-138): the same through `png_image_begin_read_from_stdio` (a real\n  `FILE*` from `fopen`) and `png_image_begin_read_from_file` (a real path under\n  `target/`). Use `libc`-style `extern \"C\" { fn fopen(..); fn fclose(..); }`\n  declarations in your own file (there is no `libc` crate available offline).\n- `write_formats` (C-139): `png_image_write_to_memory` (both as a size query with\n  a NULL buffer and with a real buffer that is exactly big enough, one byte too\n  small, and much bigger), `png_image_write_to_stdio`, `png_image_write_to_file`,\n  over every input format × `convert_to_8bit` 0/1 × colormap present/absent ×\n  `row_stride` positive and negative. Compare the produced PNG bytes exactly.\n- `round_trip` (C-140): write with the simplified API, read back with the\n  simplified API, in every format; compare.\n\nAlso cover the simplified API's own error paths (ERRORS.md rows in pngread.c /\npngwrite.c): `image.version` wrong (0, 2, 0xffffffff), `image.opaque` non-NULL on\nentry, a format with undefined bits set, `width`/`height` 0 or huge,\n`colormap_entries` > 256, NULL `memory`, NULL `image`, a colormapped format with\na NULL colormap, `png_image_free` called twice, `png_image_finish_read` without a\npreceding begin.\n\n## Rules\n- Record aggressively; a value you do not record cannot diverge visibly.\n- Use `assert_same` normally; use `assert_same_forked` (from\n  `tests/common/forked.rs`) for anything that might crash. Prefer forked for the\n  NULL/garbage error cases.\n- Fixed `Rng` seeds.\n- Iterate: `timeout 600 ./check.sh --test simplified 2>&1 | tail -40` until green.\n- If C and Rust diverge: first rule out a bug in your own test (wrong buffer size\n  — recompute it exactly as `PNG_IMAGE_BUFFER_SIZE` does; comparing bytes libpng\n  never writes; a dangling `FILE*`). Only then read the C and fix the RUST side in\n  `src/` with small surgical `Edit` calls. Never touch `c_src/`.\n- Do not edit anything in `tests/common/` — other agents are working there.\n\n## Report back\n- the list of `#[test]` fns and the CONFIGS rows each covers\n- `wc -l tests/simplified.rs`\n- the number of differential comparisons performed (count them)\n- the final `cargo test` result line\n- EVERY divergence found, with C source location, the wrong Rust code, and the fix","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-CVzjKq/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-CVzjKq-translated-rust/309de29f-cb7a-4138-9016-7ab2e7ef6079/tasks/a96f911cb79e1c046.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
