{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_lglkz5i3wqykdwng7oin3o4hmqfpqecrokraedr3ngr57vpo6otq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01UP6NJVScwKVWsWLKn6DXBk","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write high-level API tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"You are working in `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-CVzjKq/translated_rust` (cd there for everything).\n\nlibpng C-to-Rust translation. `c_src/` = ORIGINAL C, ground truth, **NEVER modify anything under `c_src/`**. `src/` = the Rust translation. A differential harness already dlopens BOTH `.so`s and compares them.\n\n## Read first (mandatory)\n1. `tests/HARNESS.md`\n2. `tests/common/mod.rs`, `tests/common/helpers.rs`, `tests/common/forked.rs`, `tests/common/types.rs`\n3. `tests/write_read.rs` — canonical example, match its style\n4. `tests/common/api.rs` is GENERATED (never edit) — grep it for exact signatures\n5. `CONFIGS.md` — your rows are `highlevel::read_png`, `highlevel::write_png`,\n   `highlevel::round_trip`, plus `chunks::rows_and_freer` is NOT yours (another\n   agent has it) — but `png_set_rows`/`png_get_rows` interact with the high-level\n   API, so use them.\n6. The C: `png_read_png` in `c_src/src/pngread.c` and `png_write_png` in\n   `c_src/src/pngwrite.c`, in full, plus every `PNG_TRANSFORM_*` in\n   `c_src/include/png.h`.\n\n## Your task\nCreate **`tests/highlevel.rs`** with `#[test]` fns named exactly `read_png`,\n`write_png`, `round_trip`.\n\n- `read_png`: for every one of the 15 `VALID_SHAPES` × interlace NONE/ADAM7,\n  build a source file with the C low-level writer (`write_plain` in\n  `tests/common/helpers.rs`), then call `png_read_png(png, info, transforms,\n  params)` on BOTH libraries and compare: the `Guard`, every warning, the\n  `png_get_rows` output (all rows, byte for byte), and everything `png_get_*`\n  reports afterwards (`log_info` covers most of it). Run every single\n  `PNG_TRANSFORM_*` flag that is legal on read, then several hundred random\n  combinations of 2..6 flags (fixed-seed `Rng`), then the write-only flags\n  (`PNG_TRANSFORM_STRIP_FILLER*`) which `png_read_png` must reject, and\n  `params` NULL vs non-NULL.\n  Note `png_read_png` requires `PNG_INFO_IDAT`-style setup: read the C to see\n  exactly what it does with `png_set_rows` / `PNG_FREE_ROWS` and what it errors\n  on (e.g. \"Image is too high to process with png_read_png()\").\n- `write_png`: the mirror — build rows yourself, `png_set_IHDR` + `png_set_rows`,\n  then `png_write_png(png, info, transforms, params)` and compare the produced\n  file bytes. Every write-legal `PNG_TRANSFORM_*` flag singly, plus random\n  combinations, plus the read-only flags which must be rejected or ignored, over\n  every shape.\n- `round_trip`: `png_read_png` with transform T then `png_write_png` with\n  transform T' over random shapes and random (T, T') pairs; compare the rewritten\n  bytes.\n\n## Rules\n- Record aggressively: `Guard`, warnings, all rows, all `png_get_*`. A value you\n  do not record cannot diverge visibly.\n- Use `assert_same`; use `assert_same_forked` (from `tests/common/forked.rs`) for\n  anything that might crash.\n- Fixed `Rng` seeds so failures reproduce.\n- Iterate: `timeout 600 ./check.sh --test highlevel 2>&1 | tail -40` until green.\n- If C and Rust diverge: first rule out a bug in your own test. In particular\n  libpng's `big_row_buf` is `png_malloc`ed, NOT zeroed, so if a transform makes\n  the row shorter than the buffer, bytes past the real row data are\n  uninitialised heap and must not be compared; and `png_set_rows` stores a\n  pointer to YOUR memory, which must stay alive. Only then read the C and fix the\n  RUST side in `src/` with small surgical `Edit` calls. Never touch `c_src/`.\n- Do not edit anything in `tests/common/` — other agents are working there.\n\n## Report back\n- the list of `#[test]` fns and the CONFIGS rows each covers\n- `wc -l tests/highlevel.rs`\n- the number of differential comparisons performed (count them)\n- the final `cargo test` result line\n- EVERY divergence found, with C source location, the wrong Rust code, and the fix"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":370644,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":370644,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"309de29f-cb7a-4138-9016-7ab2e7ef6079","uuid":"af937c81-d9ac-4f1a-af80-5dd86813162c","timestamp":"2026-08-23T02:53:15.747Z"}
