backs`, `options`,\n`row_number`, `longjmp_fn`, `struct_lifecycle`, `grayscale_palette`.\n\n- `memory` (C-24): `png_malloc`, `png_calloc`, `png_malloc_warn`,\n  `png_malloc_base`, `png_malloc_array`, `png_realloc_array`, `png_free`,\n  `png_free_data` — sizes 0, 1, 8, 4096, huge, `usize::MAX`; array counts 0/1/many\n  with and without an old array; with the default allocator and with a custom\n  `png_set_mem_fn` allocator. Compare success/failure, the diagnostics, and (for\n  `png_calloc`) that the memory really is zeroed.\n- `io_state` (C-63): `png_get_io_state` and `png_get_io_chunk_type` sampled from\n  inside the read and write callbacks at every call, over a file with several\n  chunks — this produces a long trace of (io_state, chunk_type, length) triples\n  that must match exactly. Also `png_init_io` with a real `FILE*` (use\n  `extern \"C\" { fn fopen(..) -> *mut c_void; fn fclose(..); fn tmpfile() -> *mut c_void; }`\n  declared in your own file; there is no `libc` crate available offline), and\n  `png_get_io_ptr`.\n- `crc_action` (C-141): all 36 (crit, ancil) combinations of\n  `png_set_crc_action`, against (a) a file with correct CRCs, (b) a file with a\n  broken ancillary CRC, (c) a file with a broken critical (IHDR / IDAT / PLTE)\n  CRC. Use `chunk_bad_crc` / `split_chunks` from `tests/common/helpers.rs`.\n- `user_limits` (C-142): `png_set_user_limits` / `png_get_user_width_max` /\n  `png_get_user_height_max` / `png_set_chunk_cache_max` /\n  `png_get_chunk_cache_max` / `png_set_chunk_malloc_max` /\n  `png_get_chunk_malloc_max`, with limits below / equal to / above the real image\n  and chunk sizes, and 0 (unlimited).\n- `custom_alloc` (C-143): `png_create_read_struct_2` / `png_create_write_struct_2`\n  / `png_set_mem_fn` / `png_get_mem_ptr` with an allocator that logs every\n  allocation size (the *sequence of sizes* is a very strong differential signal —\n  compare it), and with an allocator that starts failing after N allocations.\n- `status_callbacks` (C-145): `png_set_read_status_fn` / `png_set_write_status_fn`\n  over interlaced and non-interlaced images of every shape.\n- `options` (C-147): `png_set_option` for every option number 0..18 (i.e. two past\n  `PNG_OPTION_NEXT`) × `PNG_OPTION_ON` / `PNG_OPTION_OFF` / other values,\n  checking the returned previous state; then verify the options that actually\n  change behaviour do so (`PNG_MAXIMUM_INFLATE_WINDOW` on a file whose zlib\n  window is too small, `PNG_SKIP_sRGB_CHECK_PROFILE` on an iCCP chunk,\n  `PNG_IGNORE_ADLER32` on a stream with a broken adler32).\n  Also `png_permit_mng_features` with every value 0..8 and its return value.\n- `row_number` (C-148): `png_get_current_row_number` /\n  `png_get_current_pass_number` sampled from the row-status callback for\n  interlaced and non-interlaced reads and writes.\n- `longjmp_fn` (C-149): `png_set_longjmp_fn` with `jmp_buf_size` smaller than,\n  equal to and larger than 200 (glibc's `sizeof(jmp_buf)`), called once and\n  twice, with a NULL `longjmp_fn`; compare the returned pointer's NULL-ness and\n  any diagnostics. Then `png_longjmp`.\n- `struct_lifecycle` (C-150): `png_create_png_struct`, `png_destroy_png_struct`,\n  `png_create_info_struct`, `png_info_init_3` with a `png_info_struct_size`\n  smaller than / equal to / larger than the real one, `png_destroy_info_struct`,\n  `png_destroy_read_struct` / `png_destroy_write_struct` with NULL out-params and\n  called twice, and `png_create_read_struct` with a wrong `user_png_ver` string\n  (\"1.0.0\", \"1.6.0\", \"\", a 100-char string, NULL) — read `png_user_version_check`\n  in `c_src/src/png.c` for what each does.\n- `grayscale_palette` (C-151): `png_build_grayscale_palette` for bit depth\n  1,2,4,8 and the invalid 0,3,5,16,-1,255 into a 256-entry palette initialised to\n  a known pattern; compare all 768 bytes.\n\n## Rules\n- Record aggressively; a value you do not record cannot diverge visibly.\n- Use `assert_same`; use `assert_same_forked` (from `tests/common/forked.rs`) for\n  anything that might crash or abort — a crash then becomes a compared\n  observation instead of the end of the test run. `png_destroy_*` called twice and\n  `png_info_init_3` with a bogus size are good candidates.\n- Fixed `Rng` seeds so failures reproduce; many randomised inputs per row.\n- Iterate: `timeout 600 ./check.sh --test misc 2>&1 | tail -40` until green.\n- If C and Rust diverge: first rule out a bug in your own test (uninitialised\n  memory — libpng's `big_row_buf` is `png_malloc`ed not zeroed; a dangling\n  pointer; comparing raw heap addresses, which legitimately differ between two\n  libraries — compare only NULL-ness of pointers, never their value). Only then\n  read the C and fix the RUST side in `src/` with small surgical `Edit` calls.\n  Never touch `c_src/`.\n- Do not edit anything in `tests/common/` — other agents are working there.\n\n## Report back\n- the list of `#[test]` fns and the CONFIGS rows each covers\n- `wc -l tests/misc.rs`\n- the number of differential comparisons performed (count them)\n- the final `cargo test` result line\n- EVERY divergence found, with C source location, the wrong Rust code, and the fix","uuid":"a432b678-6ccf-4f3f-908d-14e0881f6d84","session_id":"309de29f-cb7a-4138-9016-7ab2e7ef6079"}
