{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01NUib4zqM42w2FgqbwbBZqs","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Differential test harness — how to write a test\n2\t\n3\tRead this before adding a test file.  `tests/write_read.rs` is the canonical\n4\texample; `tests/smoke.rs` is the smallest one.\n5\t\n6\t## Ground rules\n7\t\n8\t* The **C code in `c_src/` is the ground truth and must never be modified.**\n9\t  If C and Rust disagree, the Rust translation in `src/` is wrong.\n10\t* Never call a Rust function directly.  Everything goes through\n11\t  `common::Api`, whose fields are function pointers resolved with\n12\t  `libloading` from the two `.so`s.  This exercises the `#[no_mangle]`\n13\t  wrappers.\n14\t* Build and run with `./check.sh --test <name>` (it rebuilds the C `.so`, the\n15\t  Rust cdylib and the setjmp shim first — plain `cargo test` may silently test\n16\t  a stale `.so`).\n17\t\n18\t## Skeleton\n19\t\n20\t```rust\n21\tmod common;\n22\tuse common::*;\n23\t\n24\t#[test]\n25\tfn my_case() {\n26\t    assert_same(\"human readable case name\", |api| unsafe {\n27\t        let mut o = Outcome::default();\n28\t        let (png, info) = new_write(api);           // or new_read(api)\n29\t        (api.png_set_write_fn)(png, core::ptr::null_mut(),\n30\t                               Some(write_cb), Some(flush_cb));\n31\t        let g = guarded(api, png, &mut || {\n32\t            // ... drive libpng here; png_error() longjmps back out of\n33\t            //     `guarded`, which returns Guard::Error(msg)\n34\t            (api.png_set_IHDR)(png, info, 4, 4, 8, PNG_COLOR_TYPE_RGB,\n35\t                               PNG_INTERLACE_NONE, PNG_COMPRESSION_TYPE_BASE,\n36\t                               PNG_FILTER_TYPE_BASE);\n37\t            (api.png_write_info)(png, info);\n38\t            (api.png_write_end)(png, info);\n39\t        });\n40\t        o.push(format!(\"guard={:?}\", g));            // record the outcome\n41\t        o.output = std::mem::take(&mut tls().output); // and the bytes written\n42\t        destroy_write(api, png, info);\n43\t        o\n44\t    });\n45\t}\n46\t```\n47\t\n48\t`assert_same` runs the closure **twice** — once with the C `Api`, once with the\n49\tRust `Api`, each with a fresh `Tls` — and asserts that\n50\t\n51\t1. the ordered event trace is identical, and\n52\t2. `Outcome::output` is byte-identical.\n53\t\n54\tIt panics with a readable diff of the first difference.  It also fails if a\n55\tscenario recorded *nothing* (which would mean the test does not exercise\n56\tanything).\n57\t\n58\t## What to record\n59\t\n60\tAnything the library tells you.  Cheap and effective:\n61\t\n62\t* `log(\"...\")` — appends to the trace from anywhere, including from a callback.\n63\t  Prefer `log` over `o.push` when ordering relative to callbacks matters.\n64\t* `o.push(\"...\")` — appended after all callback events.\n65\t* `o.output` — the bytes to compare (written file, decoded rows, …).\n66\t* Return values, out-parameters, `png_get_*` results, `Guard`, warning text.\n67\t\n68\t**Record aggressively.** A value you do not record cannot diverge visibly.\n69\t\n70\t## Available pieces (`tests/common/`)\n71\t\n72\t| item | what it is |\n73\t|------|-----------|\n74\t| `libs()` | `&'static Libs { c: Api, rust: Api, shim: Shim }` |\n75\t| `Api` | one field per exported symbol — **all 384** of them, generated by `tools/gen_api.py` from `png.h` + `pngpriv.h`.  `grep '<name>' tests/common/api.rs` to see a signature. |\n76\t| `guarded(api, png, &mut || {...}) -> Guard` | arms libpng's error trap; `Guard::Ok` / `Guard::Error(String)` / `Guard::NoTrap` |\n77\t| `new_read` / `new_write` / `destroy_read` / `destroy_write` | create/destroy with the harness error+warning handlers installed |\n78\t| `read_cb` / `write_cb` / `flush_cb` | memory IO callbacks; input in `tls().input`, output in `tls().output` |\n79\t| `read_status_cb` / `write_status_cb` | row/pass callbacks that log |\n80\t| `user_transform_cb` | a deterministic user transform that logs and mangles the row |\n81\t| `malloc_cb` / `free_cb` | a logging allocator for `png_set_mem_fn` |\n82\t| `tls()` | per-thread `Tls { trace, input, in_pos, output, flushes, rows, counter, allocs, .. }` |\n83\t| `Rng::new(seed)` | SplitMix64: `u32() u8() below(n) range(lo,hi) bytes(n) pick(&[..]) bool()` |\n84\t| `Img::random(rng, w, h, ct, bd)` | a random image of a legal shape (+ palette) |\n85\t| `write_image` / `write_plain` / `WriteOpts` | drive a whole write; `extra` hook runs between `png_set_IHDR` and `png_write_info` |\n86\t| `read_image` / `read_plain` / `ReadOpts` / `RowMode` | drive a whole read; `setup` hook runs right after `png_read_info` |\n87\t| `log_info(api, png, info, tag)` | dump the whole IHDR/rowbytes/valid state |\n88\t| `chunk(name, data)` / `chunk_bad_crc` / `insert_before` / `insert_after_last` / `split_chunks` / `crc32` / `SIG` | build or patch a PNG datastream by hand |\n89\t| `VALID_SHAPES` | the 15 legal `(color_type, bit_depth)` pairs |\n90\t| `PNG_*` constants | in `common::types` |\n91\t\n92\t## Gotchas\n93\t\n94\t* `png_error` never returns — it `longjmp`s out of `guarded`.  Anything after\n95\t  the failing call inside the `guarded` body is skipped, in **both** libraries,\n96\t  which is exactly what we want to compare.\n97\t* After `Guard::Error` the `png_struct` may only be destroyed.\n98\t* Keep buffers alive across the call (`let v = ...; (api.f)(v.as_ptr())`) —\n99\t  a temporary would dangle.\n100\t* `png_read_row` needs `rowbytes` **after** `png_read_update_info`, which can\n101\t  grow the row (expand, gray→rgb, filler, …).\n102\t* Seed every `Rng` from a constant so failures reproduce.\n103\t* Use many randomised inputs per configuration — one hand-picked value per\n104\t  configuration is not enough.\n105\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01GWcu9bgbVggeqy4XeSbuyX","session_id":"309de29f-cb7a-4138-9016-7ab2e7ef6079","uuid":"76e1c4be-3c1b-4b25-ae4f-8ed61e818096","timestamp":"2026-08-23T02:56:06.565Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write misc/IO/limits tests"}
