{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_spctsja344xzbgo2oiesxain2ujz6l5ikemm7xfdchfswfif7vbq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`tests/chunks.rs` is complete and green.\n\n## Test functions and the CONFIGS rows they cover\n\n| `#[test]` fn | CONFIGS rows |\n|---|---|\n| `round_trip` | C-107 gAMA, C-108 cHRM (+`_fixed`/`_XYZ`/`_XYZ_fixed`), C-109 sRGB (+`sRGB_gAMA_and_cHRM`), C-111 sBIT, C-112 bKGD, plus the chunk-absent baseline for all 15 shapes and the getters' NULL-argument branches |\n| `round_trip_2` | C-113 hIST, C-114 tRNS, C-115 pHYs (+all 11 derived getters), C-116 oFFs (+all derived getters), C-117 tIME |\n| `round_trip_3` | C-110 iCCP, C-118 pCAL, C-119 sCAL (`_s`/`_fixed`/float), C-120 sPLT |\n| `round_trip_4` | C-121 tEXt, C-122 zTXt, C-123 iTXt, C-124 eXIf (+the deprecated `png_set_eXIf`/`png_get_eXIf`), C-125 cICP, C-126 cLLI, C-127 mDCV |\n| `iccp` | C-21 (`png_icc_check_header`/`_length`/`_tag_table` called directly **and** via iCCP chunks in a datastream, 26 synthetic profiles, `PNG_SKIP_sRGB_CHECK_PROFILE` ON/OFF/other) |\n| `text_compression` | C-60 |\n| `unknown` | C-128 |\n| `rows_and_freer` | C-129 |\n| `text_many` | C-130 |\n| `set_invalid` | C-65 |\n| `user_chunk_fn` | C-147 |\n| `write_order` | C-153 |\n\nEvery `round_trip*` case runs all three states the row asks for: chunk **absent**, **present once** (write → compare file bytes → read back → compare every `png_get_*` out-parameter, string-as-bytes, length and the `png_get_valid` mask after `png_read_info` *and* after `png_read_end`), and **present twice** (the raw chunk duplicated with `insert_after_last`). Write-side storage is also dumped inside the `png_write_info` hook.\n\n- `wc -l tests/chunks.rs` → **3701**\n- `test result: ok. 12 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out`\n\n## Divergences found in `src/`\n\n**None.** The Rust translation matched the C reference byte-for-byte and message-for-message on every case. All four initial failures were bugs in my own test:\n\n1. `iCCP total=132` — I passed `proflen=132` to `png_set_iCCP` while `Icc::build()` had grown the buffer to 144, so `png_get_iCCP` (which reads the length from the profile's own first 4 bytes) made me dump 12 bytes past libpng's allocation. Fixed by always passing `prof.len()`.\n2. NULL out-parameter probing segfaulted: `png_get_PLTE`, `_sBIT`, `_bKGD`, `_tIME`, `_oFFs`, `_eXIf_1`, `_sCAL`/`_sCAL_s`/`_sCAL_fixed` and `_pHYs_dpi` dereference out-params **unconditionally** once the chunk is valid. Restructured so NULL out-params are only used on an info struct where nothing is valid, and the populated struct is probed via NULL `png`/`info`.\n3. `png_get_sCAL_fixed` calls `png_fixed()`, which `png_error()`s above ~21474; the dump now skips it when the value is unrepresentable.\n4. `free_data MUL num=0` failed only under parallel test threads: `png_free_data(PNG_FREE_TEXT, num)` frees the single allocation holding `key|text|lang|lang_key` but clears **only** `key`, leaving the other three dangling. The dump now stops after `key` when `key` is NULL.\n\n## Verification that the tests actually bite\n\nBecause the suite runs fast (0.1 s), I validated it end-to-end by temporarily mutating the Rust `png_write_cLLI_fixed` (`src/gen/pngwutil_p05.rs`, `maxFALL` → `maxFALL ^ 1`): 4 of the 12 tests failed (`round_trip_4`, `rows_and_freer`, `set_invalid`, `write_order`). The mutation was reverted and the revert verified by grep, and `src/` is otherwise untouched.\n\nOne note for the caller: `tests/errors.rs` (`setter_validation`, `coverage_report`) fails in a full `./check.sh` run. That file was created by another agent while I was working and is unrelated to my changes — `--test chunks` is green on its own and in the full run."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":745,"cache_read_input_tokens":318644,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":745,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01BMWL9AwQNN8BAN8oW4HXMy","session_id":"309de29f-cb7a-4138-9016-7ab2e7ef6079","uuid":"f6d9b11a-6ddf-409a-840b-4621f243b119","timestamp":"2026-08-23T03:02:33.134Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write chunks differential tests"}
