{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_yr4hv3cklrprzpdozysz6uqk5otgt7bfry53lpobmboahojhmtoa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `tests/simplified.rs` is written and green.\n\n## Test functions and CONFIGS rows\n\n| `#[test]` fn | CONFIGS.md row | entry points |\n|---|---|---|\n| `read_formats` | **C-138** (`simplified::read_formats`) | `png_image_begin_read_from_memory` + `png_image_finish_read` + `png_image_free` |\n| `read_stdio` | **C-139** (`simplified::read_stdio`) | `png_image_begin_read_from_stdio` (real `FILE*` via `fopen`) + `png_image_begin_read_from_file` (real path under `target/simplified/`) |\n| `write_formats` | **C-140** (`simplified::write_formats`) | `png_image_write_to_memory` (size query / exact / one-byte-short / zero-length / `PNG_IMAGE_PNG_SIZE_MAX`), `png_image_write_to_stdio`, `png_image_write_to_file` |\n| `round_trip` | **C-141** (`simplified::round_trip`) | simplified write → simplified read → simplified write |\n\nNote: the task brief numbered these C-137…C-140; the actual rows in `CONFIGS.md` are **C-138…C-141**. I ticked those four rows `[x]`.\n\nAll four also cover configuration axis **S. simplified formats**.\n\n## Numbers\n\n- `wc -l tests/simplified.rs` → **2000**\n- **102,868 differential comparisons** (measured, single-threaded): `read_formats` 79,730 · `read_stdio` 9,352 · `round_trip` 6,071 · `write_formats` 7,715. Of these **80 are `assert_same_forked`** (all NULL/garbage/tampered-struct cases), the rest `assert_same`.\n- Sanity counters built into the test: 134,962 `png_image_finish_read` calls returned success and 134,938 of those left a buffer that differs from the pre-fill pattern; 10,354 successful `png_image_write_*` calls. So the suite is not silently agreeing on error paths.\n- Final result line: `test result: ok. 4 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 9.42s`\n\nRecorded per call: return value, `opaque` nullness, `version`, `width`, `height`, `format`, `flags`, `colormap_entries`, `warning_or_error`, the message text in the trace **and all 64 raw `message` bytes appended to `Outcome::output`**, plus every byte of the pixel buffer and of the 256-entry colormap (both pre-filled with a deterministic pattern so untouched bytes are compared too). Buffer sizes are computed with the exact `PNG_IMAGE_SAMPLE_*` / `PNG_IMAGE_PIXEL_*` / `PNG_IMAGE_ROW_STRIDE` / `PNG_IMAGE_BUFFER_SIZE` / `PNG_IMAGE_COLORMAP_SIZE` / `PNG_IMAGE_PNG_SIZE_MAX` (incl. `PNG_ZLIB_MAX_SIZE`, `PNG_ZBUF_SIZE=8192`) formulas transcribed from `png.h`.\n\n## Divergences found\n\n**One**, and it is C undefined behaviour rather than a translation bug, so `src/` was left untouched:\n\n- `png_image_write_to_memory/stdio/file` with `image.width == 0`. `png_image_write_main` (`c_src/src/pngwrite.c:2044`) evaluates `image->height > 0xffffffffU/png_row_stride` with `png_row_stride == image->width * channels == 0` → **integer division by zero**. The C library dies with **SIGFPE (8)**; the verbatim Rust translation (`src/gen/pngwrite_p05.rs:244`, `if (*image).height > 0xffffffffu32 / png_row_stride`) panics with \"attempt to divide by zero\" → **SIGABRT (6)** under `panic = \"abort\"`. Both crash, but with different signals, so `assert_same_forked` cannot be satisfied.\n  `TRANSLATION_NOTES.md` explicitly prescribes this translation (\"Division/modulo by a value that could be 0 must be reproduced verbatim (the C code never does this on a valid path)\"), and reproducing SIGFPE from Rust would need raw `div` inline asm. The two `width == 0` write cases are therefore excluded, with the reasoning recorded in a comment next to the `bad` table in `write_formats`. Everything reachable *without* dividing by zero is still covered: `height == 0`, `width == 0x7fffffff`, `width == 0xffffffff`, `0x10000 × 0x10000`, stride-too-small, negative stride, and on the read side `finish_read` with `width`/`height` 0 or `0xffffffff` (there `image->opaque == NULL` short-circuits the division away).\n\nNo other divergence: the Rust simplified API matched the C byte for byte on all 102,868 comparisons, so **no edits were made to `src/`** (verified `cmp`-clean against pre-experiment copies) and nothing under `c_src/` was touched.\n\n## Harness self-validation\n\nTo prove the test discriminates rather than agreeing vacuously, I temporarily injected two 1-LSB mutations into the Rust library and confirmed both were caught, then reverted and rebuilt:\n- `src/gen/pngwrite_p04.rs:237` `wrapping_add(16384)` → `16383` (the un-premultiply rounding in `png_write_image_16bit`) → `write_formats` and `round_trip` FAILED. The first run only `round_trip` caught it (the rounding differs for ~1 component value in 32768), so I added `write_formats` section 1b: a 256×200 image for the four `LINEAR_*` formats specifically to give that path enough samples.\n- `src/gen/pngread_p07.rs:95` `(231 * gray + 128) >> 8` → `+ 127` → `read_formats` and `read_stdio` FAILED.\n\n## Coverage side-effects\n\n`png_safe_error` copies trapped `png_error` text into `png_image::message` instead of routing it through the harness' error callback, so those diagnostics were invisible to `tools/error_coverage.py`. `snap()`/`state_raw()` now call `observe()` on any non-zero `warning_or_error`, which makes 18 previously-unreached simplified-API rejection sites show up as verified, including all eleven per-colour-type `\"… color-map: too few entries\"` sites (`pngread.c:2056, 2135, 2233, 2267, 2301, 2406, 2422, 2530, 2579, 2664, 2695`) plus `pngread.c:1427`, `pngread.c:3925` and `pngwrite.c:2045, 2049, 2053, 2072, 2156`. Those are driven by a dedicated sweep that starves `colormap_entries` (0…0xffffffff) after a successful `begin_read` for all 15 source shapes × 13 colour-mapped output formats.\n\nKey files: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-CVzjKq/translated_rust/tests/simplified.rs`, `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-CVzjKq/translated_rust/CONFIGS.md` (rows C-138…C-141 ticked)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":388,"cache_read_input_tokens":261794,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":388,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01DkTVAznv6jg5QHC72BbbtR","session_id":"309de29f-cb7a-4138-9016-7ab2e7ef6079","uuid":"dc04a919-a2c4-4578-befe-06fb923e623e","timestamp":"2026-08-23T03:24:53.040Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write simplified API tests"}
