{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_hlhvbw3greuvjuzlzlzzjdk5jezjesd32huk6zihokwp66sjkycq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`tests/misc.rs` is complete and green. Summary:\n\n## Tests and CONFIGS rows\n\n| `#[test]` fn | CONFIGS row | comparisons |\n|---|---|---|\n| `memory` | C-23 (`png_malloc/calloc/malloc_warn/malloc_base/malloc_array/realloc_array/free/free_data`) | 202 |\n| `io_state` | C-64 (`png_get_io_state/io_chunk_type/init_io/get_io_ptr`) | 45 |\n| `crc_action` | C-142 (`png_set_crc_action`) | 431 |\n| `user_limits` | C-143 (`png_set_user_limits`, chunk cache/malloc max) | 111 |\n| `custom_alloc` | C-144 (`png_create_*_struct_2`, `png_set_mem_fn`, `png_get_mem_ptr`) | 96 |\n| `status_callbacks` | C-146 (`png_set_read/write_status_fn`) | 86 |\n| `options` | C-148 (`png_set_option`, `png_permit_mng_features`, `png_reset_zstream`) | 365 |\n| `row_number` | C-149 (`png_get_current_row/pass_number`) | 141 |\n| `longjmp_fn` | C-150 (`png_set_longjmp_fn`, `png_longjmp`, `png_free_jmpbuf`) | 180 |\n| `struct_lifecycle` | C-151 (create/init/destroy of both structs, `png_user_version_check`) | 49 |\n| `grayscale_palette` | C-152 (`png_build_grayscale_palette`) | 55 |\n\n- `wc -l tests/misc.rs` → **3983**\n- **1761 differential comparisons** total (1720 in-process `assert_same`, 41 `assert_same_forked` across 9 forked sites: NULL `FILE*` reads, the 28 failing-allocator budgets, 4 `png_longjmp`→`PNG_ABORT` cases, `png_info_init_3(NULL,..)`, `png_create_png_struct` OOM, double destroy).\n- Final result line: `test result: ok. 11 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 11.11s`\n\n## Divergences found\n\n**None.** No file under `src/` needed changing; `c_src/` and `tests/common/` were not touched. The comparison is genuinely discriminating — verified with a negative control (a scenario that pushes an extra trace entry only for the Rust `Api` is correctly reported as `event traces differ at index 0`), and by inspecting recorded traces:\n\n- The custom-allocator **allocation-size sequences match exactly**, including `sizeof(png_struct) = 1232` and `sizeof(png_info) = 352`, over all 15 shapes × both interlace modes for write and read, and over a chunk-heavy file that drives `png_malloc_array`/`png_realloc_array`.\n- The IO-state traces are long and correct (`0x0011 sig → 0x0021 hdr → 0x0041 data → 0x0081 crc` per chunk, with the chunk name).\n- `PNG_MAXIMUM_INFLATE_WINDOW` is provably exercised: a stream whose zlib CINFO is 8 gives `\"IDAT: invalid window size (libpng)\"` with the option off and `\"IDAT: invalid window size\"` (zlib's) with it on — both libraries agree on both.\n- The MNG intrapixel path round-trips: writing with `png_set_sig_bytes(8)` + `PNG_FLAG_MNG_FILTER_64` + `PNG_INTRAPIXEL_DIFFERENCING` and reading back reproduces the pixels exactly (so `png_do_write_intrapixel` / `png_do_read_intrapixel` are both covered), while `mng=0` rejects with `\"Invalid IHDR data\"`.\n\n## Notes on the build configuration (not bugs)\n\n- `PNG_DISABLE_ADLER32_CHECK_SUPPORTED` is `#undef` in `c_src/include/pnglibconf.h:30`, so `PNG_IGNORE_ADLER32` has **no effect** in this build (a broken adler32 gives `\"IDAT: incorrect data check\"` with the option on or off). The Rust side correctly compiles the same branch out (`src/gen/pngrutil_p02.rs:106`). The test still compares all four combinations.\n- `PNG_SKIP_sRGB_CHECK_PROFILE` is not referenced by any `c_src/src/*.c` in this configuration either; the option's return values and the iCCP read behaviour with it on/off are still compared.\n- `png_info_init_3`'s \"reallocated\" observation is recorded as pointer identity, which glibc's tcache makes indistinguishable (free+malloc of the same size class returns the same chunk). The real check that both libraries agree on `sizeof(png_info)` comes from the custom-allocator size log; the sweep additionally proves the struct is still usable for a full read after either branch (sizes 0/8/128/351/352/353/512/4096/`usize::MAX`).\n- `tmpfile()` is blocked by the sandbox here, so `temp_file()` falls back to `fopen(scratch_dir()/…, \"w+b\")`; `png_init_io` is still exercised with a genuine `FILE*` for both write and read."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":597,"cache_read_input_tokens":318205,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":597,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01GWcu9bgbVggeqy4XeSbuyX","session_id":"309de29f-cb7a-4138-9016-7ab2e7ef6079","uuid":"70a554e7-13b1-44d5-8599-c0a6d2c9638f","timestamp":"2026-08-23T03:31:14.925Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write misc/IO/limits tests"}
