{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"aa608d7a4ec38f8b1","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01TGCoGUz85WiUHtvgs8whHb","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-CVzjKq/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-CVzjKq-translated-rust/309de29f-cb7a-4138-9016-7ab2e7ef6079/tasks/aa608d7a4ec38f8b1.output","summary":"Done. `tests/progressive.rs` is new; nothing under `c_src/` and nothing in `tests/common/` was touched, and no change to `src/` was needed.\n\n## Tests and CONFIGS rows\n\n| `#[test]` fn | CONFIGS row | comparisons |\n|---|---|---|\n| `chunk_sizes` | C-134 (`png_set_progressive_read_fn`, `png_process_data`, `png_progressive_combine_row`, `png_get_progressive_ptr`) | 1170 |\n| `pause_skip` | C-135 (`png_process_data_pause`, `png_process_data_skip`) | 90 |\n| `split_boundaries` | C-136 (`png_push_read_chunk` / `_IDAT` / `_save_buffer` / `_restore_buffer` / `_fill_buffer` boundaries) + the `pngpread.c` error paths | 1024 |\n| `transforms` | C-137 (read transforms installed from the info callback) | 1252 |\n\n- `wc -l tests/progressive.rs` → **2267**\n- **3536 differential comparisons** (each test prints its own count; 2 of them are `assert_same_forked`)\n- `test result: ok. 4 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 1.63s`\n- Full suite (`./check.sh`): all 12 test binaries pass, `CONFIGS.md: 154/154 rows covered by a passing test`, `ERROR_COVERAGE.md: 242/318 (76%)`.\n\n## Divergences found\n\n**None.** The `pngpread.c` translation (`src/gen/pngpread_p01.rs`, `pngpread_p02.rs`) is byte-faithful over everything these 3536 cases reach, including the `num_to_check - 4` `size_t` wrap-around in `png_push_read_sig`, the `PNG_PUSH_SAVE_BUFFER_IF_*` boundaries, the `png_read_push_finish_row` pass-skipping loop and the stale contents of the calloc'd interlaced `big_row_buf`.\n\nTo show the suite is actually sensitive rather than vacuously green, I mutation-tested it and reverted:\n- `pass == 5 && width < 2` → `< 3` in `png_read_push_finish_row` → caught by `chunk_sizes`;\n- `PNG_PUSH_SAVE_BUFFER_IF_FULL` `+4` → `+3` and `buffer_size < 8` → `< 7` in `png_push_read_chunk`/`_IDAT` → caught by **all four** tests.\n(`wrapping_sub(4)` → `saturating_sub(4)` in `png_push_read_sig` is *not* caught, and provably cannot be: the inner `png_sig_cmp` range is always a superset of the range the outer call already found mismatching, so both spellings return non-zero for every reachable input.)\n\n`chunk_sizes` also asserts the fully combined image equals the image that was written, so the comparison is anchored to ground truth and not just \"both agree on nothing\".\n\n## Notable findings about the C\n\n1. **`png_process_data_skip` is a stub in this version** — there is no `PNG_SKIP_MODE` anywhere in `c_src/src/pngpread.c`; lines 91-102 only call `png_app_warning(...)` and `return 0`. And because `c_src/include/png.h:310` has `PNG_LIBPNG_BUILD_BASE_TYPE == PNG_LIBPNG_BUILD_BETA`, `PNG_RELEASE_BUILD` is 0, so `png_create_read_struct` (`pngread.c:67`) does *not* set `PNG_FLAG_APP_WARNINGS_WARN` — `png_process_data_skip` is therefore **fatal** unless the app called `png_set_benign_errors(1)`. Tested with default flags and with `png_set_benign_errors(0)`/`(1)`, standalone and after every feed, plus `skip(NULL)` (which segfaults inside `png_app_warning` — compared in a forked child).\n2. **`png_process_data_pause` must not be called from the row callback.** `png_push_read_IDAT` (`pngpread.c:455`/`481`) unconditionally does `png_ptr->buffer_size -= save_size` after `png_process_IDAT_data` returns; a pause inside the row callback has already set `buffer_size = 0`, so that underflows and `png_process_data`'s `while (png_ptr->buffer_size)` walks off the end of the caller's buffer. The pause is only well-defined from `info_fn`/`end_fn` (which `png_push_read_chunk` returns from with no further buffer arithmetic) and after the call — so the test pauses from those three places, with `save` 0 and 1, rewinding the returned byte count and resuming until the file is consumed (asserted to have actually returned a non-zero count).\n3. **Harness hazard worth knowing about:** `log_info`'s `png_get_IHDR` calls `png_check_IHDR`, which is *fatal* on an info struct that never saw an IHDR (e.g. a stream truncated to 0 bytes) and on some legitimate post-transform states. A `png_error` raised outside `guarded` runs `png_default_error` and then `longjmp`s onto the dead `harness_run` stack frame, taking the whole test binary down (I hit exactly this). Fixed locally by running the post-feed introspection under its own `guarded`, and by adding a `log_shape` helper that records the same fields through the individual pure accessors.\n\n## Error paths asserted-reached (self-checking)\n\n`split_boundaries` and `transforms` end by diffing `observed()` against a required list, so a future refactor cannot silently stop reaching them: ERRORS.md **D-68, D-69, D-70, D-71, D-72, D-73, D-77, D-79, D-80, D-82, D-83, D-84, D-85, D-86**, plus `PNG unsigned integer out of range` (the `png_get_uint_31` header parse that only the progressive reader performs), `CRC error`, and D-67/R-92 (`png_process_data_skip`). D-74/D-75/D-76 (`save_buffer` OOM/overflow) and D-78 (`No IDAT data (internal error)`) are unreachable from outside the library.","usage":{"total_tokens":304293,"tool_uses":128,"duration_ms":3227710},"uuid":"595e97a1-d156-4de5-a5f6-33d60c954e53","session_id":"309de29f-cb7a-4138-9016-7ab2e7ef6079"}
