{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_zncgjafqywgayiugrmzmffewfwbijdiomu7b4mwesglbot4hpioq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01Q2LumuFA2ZNcudyRk6z47M","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Close remaining error-surface gaps","subagent_type":"general-purpose","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"You are working in `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-CVzjKq/translated_rust` (cd there for everything).\n\nlibpng C-to-Rust translation. `c_src/` = ORIGINAL C, ground truth, **NEVER modify anything under `c_src/`**. `src/` = the Rust translation. A differential harness dlopens BOTH `.so`s and compares them.\n\n## Read first (mandatory)\n1. `tests/HARNESS.md`\n2. `tests/common/mod.rs`, `tests/common/helpers.rs`, `tests/common/forked.rs`, `tests/common/types.rs`\n3. `tests/errors.rs` — the existing error-path test file; match its style, and reuse its\n   ideas (`with_c`, `base_png`, `diff_read`, `chunk`, `insert_before`, `chunk_bad_crc`,\n   a failing allocator, `assert_same_forked`).\n4. `ERROR_COVERAGE.md` — the machine-generated report of which of libpng's 318\n   checkable diagnostic sites the suite has reached (currently 242/318).\n5. `tests/common/api.rs` is GENERATED (never edit) — grep it for exact signatures.\n   NOTE: it exports **all 384 symbols**, including internal ones like\n   `png_write_IHDR`, `png_write_iTXt`, `png_write_tIME`, `png_write_sCAL_s`,\n   `png_write_iCCP`, `png_write_sPLT`, `png_read_start_row`, `png_do_read_transformations`.\n   Calling those *directly* is often the only way to reach a check that the public\n   setters would have rejected earlier — that is legitimate and desirable here.\n\n## Your task\nCreate **`tests/errors_deep.rs`** whose only purpose is to make the C library\nproduce the diagnostics listed below and prove the Rust library produces exactly\nthe same thing. For EACH item: read the C at that exact file:line, work out the\nprecise input that reaches it, and write a differential test. Use `assert_same`\nnormally and `assert_same_forked` for anything that might crash.\n\nTarget sites (file:line — message):\n\n- `pngerror.c:593` \"Libpng jmp_buf still allocated\" and `pngerror.c:600`\n  \"Application jmp_buf size changed\" — `png_set_longjmp_fn` with a size larger\n  than `sizeof(jmp_buf)` (200) and then a *different* size; read\n  `png_set_longjmp_fn` / `png_free_jmpbuf`.\n- `pngread.c:444` \"Invalid attempt to read row data\" — `png_read_row` when\n  `png_ptr->row_buf` is NULL.\n- `pngread.c:729` \".Too many IDATs found\" and `pngread.c:747` \"..Too many IDATs\n  found\" — read `png_read_end`; note the leading dots are `PNG_STRING_NEWLINE`\n  concatenation artefacts, so grep the C for the surrounding literals.\n- `pngrtran.c:120` \"invalid after png_start_read_image or png_read_update_info\"\n  and `pngtrans.c:845` \"info change after png_start_read_image or\n  png_read_update_info\" — call a `png_set_*` transform (and a `png_set_<chunk>`)\n  AFTER `png_read_update_info`.\n- `pngrtran.c:1886` \"invalid background gamma type\" — `png_set_background_fixed`\n  with a `background_gamma_code` outside 0..3 (and `PNG_BACKGROUND_GAMMA_UNKNOWN`).\n- `pngrtran.c:2104` \"Palette is NULL in indexed image\" — read\n  `png_init_read_transformations`; a palette image whose PLTE never arrived\n  (e.g. `png_set_expand` + a datastream with a 0-length or missing PLTE).\n- `pngrutil.c:211` \"bad header (invalid length)\" — `png_read_chunk_header` with a\n  declared chunk length > `PNG_UINT_31_MAX`. Check whether `png_get_uint_31`\n  fires first and, if so, find the path that reaches line 211.\n- `pngrutil.c:789` and `pngrutil.c:1455` \"extra compressed data\" — a zTXt / iCCP\n  whose zlib stream ends before the chunk data does.\n- `pngrutil.c:1577` \"No space in chunk cache for sPLT\" — `png_set_chunk_cache_max`\n  small plus several sPLT chunks.\n- `pngrutil.c:1635` \"sPLT chunk too long\".\n- `pngrutil.c:2316` \"bad height format\" and `pngrutil.c:2319` \"non-positive\n  height\" — an sCAL chunk with a well-formed width and a malformed / zero /\n  negative height.\n- `pngrutil.c:3478` \"invalid user transform pixel depth\" —\n  `png_set_user_transform_info` with a bit depth / channel count that makes the\n  pixel depth illegal.\n- `pngset.c:1407` \"invalid location in png_set_unknown_chunks\" and `pngset.c:1540`\n  \"invalid unknown chunk location\" — read the C for exactly which `png_ptr->mode`\n  and `location` combinations reach each.\n- `pngset.c:1681` \"png_set_keep_unknown_chunks: too many chunks\" — a very large\n  `num_chunks`.\n- `pngset.c:950` \"Insufficient memory to store text\" — the failing allocator plus\n  `png_set_text`; find the allocation index that reaches this exact line.\n- `pngwio.c:60` \"Write Error\" — `png_init_io` with a `FILE*` that fails to write.\n  `/dev/full` may not be available in the sandbox; a file opened `\"rb\"` (read\n  only) makes `fwrite` fail immediately, which is simpler. Confirm the C really\n  reaches the message before asserting.\n- `pngwutil.c:200` \"length exceeds PNG maximum\" — `png_write_chunk_start` with a\n  length > `PNG_UINT_31_MAX`.\n- `pngwutil.c:773` \"Invalid compression type specified\" and `pngwutil.c:804`\n  \"Invalid interlace type specified\" — call the exported `png_write_IHDR`\n  directly with a bad compression / interlace type.\n- `pngwutil.c:1148` \"Profile length does not match profile\" and `pngwutil.c:1154`\n  \"iCCP: invalid keyword\" — `png_set_iCCP` with a profile whose embedded length\n  field disagrees with `proflen`, and with a keyword `png_check_keyword` mangles\n  to nothing. If `png_set_iCCP` rejects first, call `png_write_iCCP` directly.\n- `pngwutil.c:1194` \"sPLT: invalid keyword\" — likewise via `png_write_sPLT`.\n- `pngwutil.c:1692` \"iTXt: invalid compression\" — via `png_write_iTXt` directly.\n- `pngwutil.c:1862` \"Can't write sCAL (buffer too small)\" — `png_set_sCAL_s` with\n  very long width/height strings.\n- `pngwutil.c:1912` \"Invalid time specified for tIME chunk\" — via\n  `png_write_tIME` directly with an out-of-range `png_time`.\n- `png.c:3634` \"gamma table being rebuilt\" — read `png_build_gamma_table`; reach\n  it by making the gamma tables be built twice.\n- `pngpread.c:562` \"Decompression error in IDAT\" — the progressive reader on a\n  datastream whose IDAT zlib data is corrupt (repair the CRC so the zlib layer is\n  what rejects it).\n- `pngread.c:1643` \"color-map index out of range\", `pngread.c:3960`\n  \"png_image_read: alpha channel lost\", `pngread.c:3986` \"unexpected alpha swap\n  transformation\", `pngread.c:3994` \"png_read_image: invalid transformations\" —\n  the simplified read API; see `tests/simplified.rs` for how it is driven.\n- `pngwutil.c:1589` \"tEXt: text too long\", `pngwutil.c:1736` \"iTXt: uncompressed\n  text too long\", `pngrutil.c:4649` \"Row has too many bytes to allocate in\n  memory\", `png.c:2007` \"Image width is too large for this architecture\",\n  `pngset.c:1832` \"Compression buffer size limited to system maximum\" — these\n  need a >2 GiB object or 32-bit `size_t`. Verify from the C that they are\n  unreachable on this 64-bit build and, instead of a test, add a comment in the\n  file explaining precisely why (quote the comparison and the constant values).\n\n## Then\n1. Run `timeout 600 ./check.sh --test errors_deep 2>&1 | tail -40` until green.\n2. Run the WHOLE suite once: `timeout 3000 ./check.sh > /tmp/full.log 2>&1; tail -5 /tmp/full.log`\n   and report the new `ERROR_COVERAGE.md` number (it must go UP from 242/318).\n3. At the end of your test file, add a `#[test] fn reached_the_intended_sites()`\n   that asserts each message you were able to reach really was observed (use\n   `observed()` from the harness, like `tests/progressive.rs` does), so a future\n   refactor cannot silently stop reaching them.\n\n## Rules\n- If C and Rust DIVERGE: first rule out a bug in your own test (uninitialised\n  memory — libpng's `big_row_buf` is `png_malloc`ed, not zeroed; dangling\n  pointers; buffers shorter than the length you told libpng about). Only then read\n  the C and fix the RUST side in `src/` with small surgical `Edit` calls. Never\n  touch `c_src/`.\n- Do NOT edit anything in `tests/common/`, any other `tests/*.rs`, or `tools/`.\n- Fixed `Rng` seeds.\n\n## Report back\n- for EACH target site: reached (with the exact message text) or unreachable (with\n  the C reasoning)\n- `wc -l tests/errors_deep.rs`, the test result line, and the new\n  `ERROR_COVERAGE.md` count\n- EVERY divergence found, with C source location, the wrong Rust code, and the fix"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2075,"cache_read_input_tokens":500413,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2075,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"309de29f-cb7a-4138-9016-7ab2e7ef6079","uuid":"d1ca0e76-1b9d-4b5b-ae38-a1e8891f8ce7","timestamp":"2026-08-23T04:02:10.565Z"}
