{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01AJNqiFNBBiMwc2gYBUbujW","type":"tool_result","content":"#!/bin/bash\n# Build everything the differential tests need, then run them.\n#   ./check.sh                 -- all tests\n#   ./check.sh --test errors   -- one test target\nset -e\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\"\nif [ ! -f c_src/build/libpng.so ]; then\n    mkdir -p c_src/build\n    (cd c_src/build && cmake .. -DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON >/dev/null && cmake --build . -j8 >/dev/null)\nfi\ncargo build --offline --release\n# every test binary appends the diagnostics it observed here; start each run clean\nrm -rf target/observed\nmkdir -p target/observed\ncargo test --offline --release \"$@\" 2>&1 | tee target/test_output.txt\nrc=${PIPESTATUS:-$?}\ngrep -E '^test result:' target/test_output.txt || true\n# whole-suite ERRORS.md coverage (each integration test is its own process)\npython3 tools/error_coverage.py || true\n# CONFIGS.md row coverage\npython3 tools/config_coverage.py || true\nexit $rc\nc_exports.txt\nconfig_coverage.py\nerror_coverage.py\ngen_api.py\ngen_configs_rows.py\ngen_error_sites.py\ngen_errors.py\ngen_sweep.py\n# ERROR_COVERAGE.md — which ERRORS.md rows the tests actually reached\n\nGenerated by `tools/error_coverage.py` from `tests/error_sites.txt` (all\n368 diagnostic call sites in `c_src/src/*.c`) and `target/observed/*.txt`\n(every diagnostic the differential tests made **both** libraries emit).\n\nA site is marked `x` only if the suite observed its message coming out of\nboth libraries with identical traces — `assert_same` / `assert_same_forked`\ncompare *before* the message is recorded, so a recorded message is by\nconstruction one the two libraries agreed on.\n\n| | count |\n|---|---|\n| diagnostic call sites in the C sources | 368 |\n| … with a literal message (checkable) | 318 |\n| … whose message is assembled at run time | 50 |\n| **sites reached by the differential tests** | **242 (76%)** |\n| distinct d