{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_017HJMYWqeYBHwQj56YB9XoU","type":"tool_result","content":"22\t//!\n23\t//! Five of the targeted sites are dead code on a 64-bit `size_t`; they are\n24\t//! documented here (with the comparison and the constants) instead of tested,\n25\t//! because reaching them needs either a >2 GiB object or a 32-bit `size_t`:\n26\t//!\n27\t//! * `pngwutil.c:1589` \"tEXt: text too long\" —\n28\t//!   `if (text_len > PNG_UINT_31_MAX - (key_len+1)) png_error(...)`.\n29\t//!   `text_len = strlen(text)` and `key_len <= 79`, so the trigger is a NUL\n30\t//!   terminated string of more than `0x7fffffff - 80 == 2147483567` bytes.\n31\t//!\n32\t//! * `pngwutil.c:1736` \"iTXt: uncompressed text too long\" —\n33\t//!   `if (comp.input_len > PNG_UINT_31_MAX-prefix_len) png_error(...)`, where\n34\t//!   `comp.input_len = strlen(text)` and `prefix_len <= 81 + lang + lang_key`.\n35\t//!   Again a >2 GiB C string.\n36\t//!\n37\t//! * `pngrutil.c:4649` \"Row has too many bytes to allocate in memory\" —\n38\t//!   `if (png_ptr->rowbytes > (PNG_SIZE_MAX - 1)) png_error(...)`.\n39\t//!   `PNG_SIZE_MAX` is `((size_t)(-1))` = 2^64-1 here, while\n40\t//!   `rowbytes = PNG_ROWBYTES(pixel_depth, width)` is at most\n41\t//!   `(2^31-1) * (64/8) == 17179869176` — 30 bits short of the limit.\n42\t//!\n43\t//! * `png.c:2007` \"Image width is too large for this architecture\" — the test at\n44\t//!   png.c:1989 is\n45\t//!\n46\t//!   ```c\n47\t//!       if (((width + 7) & ~(png_alloc_size_t)7) >\n48\t//!           (((PNG_SIZE_MAX - 48 /* big_row_buf hack */\n49\t//!                           - 1) /* filter byte */\n50\t//!                           / 8) /* 8-byte RGBA pixels */\n51\t//!                           - 1))/* extra max_pixel_depth pad */\n52\t//!   ```\n53\t//!\n54\t//!   i.e. `> ((2^64-1 - 49) / 8) - 1 == 2305843009213693902`, while `width` is a\n55\t//!   `png_uint_32`, so the left-hand side is at most `4294967302 & ~7`.  Ten\n56\t//!   orders of magnitude short.  (The `width > PNG_UINT_31_MAX` warning at\n57\t//!   png.c:1977 does *not* short-circuit this one — it only sets `error = 1` —\n58\t//!   so the branch really is evaluated on every call and is simply never true.)\n59\t//!\n60\t//! * `pngset.c:1832` \"Compression buffer size limited to system maximum\" —\n61\t//!   `if (size > ZLIB_IO_MAX) { png_warning(...); size = ZLIB_IO_MAX; }` where\n62\t//!   `ZLIB_IO_MAX` is `((uInt)-1)` = 4294967295 (pngstruct.h:53).  A `size_t`\n63\t//!   larger than that *is* representable on this target, so this one is\n64\t//!   reachable — and `errors.rs::write_option_errors` already reaches it with\n65\t//!   `png_set_compression_buffer_size(png, usize::MAX)`.  It is listed here only\n66\t//!   because on a 32-bit `size_t` the comparison would be the dead one.\n67\t//!\n68\t//! Three more of the targeted sites are dead for a different reason, each\n69\t//! documented on the test that pins down what happens instead:\n70\t//!\n71\t//! * `pngrutil.c:211` \"bad header (invalid length)\" — shadowed by the identical\n72\t//!   condition inside `png_get_uint_31`, 14 lines earlier; see\n73\t//!   `chunk_header_invalid_length`.\n74\t//! * `pngwutil.c:1148` \"Profile length does not match profile\" — shadowed by the\n75\t//!   literally identical `if` at pngwutil.c:1137; see `iccp_write_direct`.\n76\t//! * `pngrutil.c:1635` \"sPLT chunk too long\" — a 64-bit `PNG_SIZE_MAX`\n77\t//!   comparison against a value bounded by the chunk length; see\n78\t//!   `splt_chunk_cache`.\n79\t#![allow(non_snake_case)]\n80\t\n81\tmod common;\n82\t\n83\tuse common::*;\n84\tuse core::ffi::{c_char, c_int, c_void};\n85\t\n86\t/* ================================================================== */\n87\t/* small local helpers                                                 */\n88\t/* ================================================================== */\n89\t\n90\t/// Run `f` against the C library with a fresh `Tls`; used to manufacture the\n91\t/// *valid* datastreams that the read-side cases then mutate.\n92\tfn with_c<T>(f: impl FnOnce(&Api) -> T) -> T {\n93\t    let l = libs();\n94\t    let mut state = Box::new(Tls::default());\n95\t    let prev = set_tls(&mut *state as *mut Tls);\n96\t    let prev_api = set_cur_api(&l.c as *const Api);\n97\t    let r = f(&l.c);\n98\t    set_cur_api(prev_api);\n99\t    set_tls(prev);\n100\t    r\n101\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Q2LumuFA2ZNcudyRk6z47M","session_id":"309de29f-cb7a-4138-9016-7ab2e7ef6079","uuid":"631f155b-8b72-4fc6-a163-04c1e76f9f91","timestamp":"2026-08-23T04:46:23.708Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Close remaining error-surface gaps"}
