[unoptimized + debuginfo] target(s) in 0.01s\n=== freshness ===\n-rwxr-xr-x. 1 scheschb amazon 314040 Aug 23 05:17 c_src/build/libpng.so\n-rwxr-xr-x. 2 scheschb amazon 730256 Aug 23 03:27 target/release/liblibpng.so\n=== git-style summary of what changed in src/ ===\nsrc/ffi.rs\nsrc/gen/pngrtran_p03.rs\nsrc/gen/pngset_p01.rs\nsrc/gen/pngwrite_p05.rs\nsrc/util.rs","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_52xad6fgfw6jzsaulj3rrbdzxwdadoy7egzn727yv5irpdecirca","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Here's the summary.\n\n## What was verified\n\nlibpng 1.6.59 (~30 k lines of C → ~35 k lines of Rust). Both libraries are `dlopen`ed and driven **only** through `dlsym`, so the `#[no_mangle]` export wrappers are part of what's tested.\n\n**Phase A artifacts** (all mechanically generated, regenerated by `./check.sh`):\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | 384 C symbols vs 384 Rust — **0 missing, 0 extra, 0 type mismatches**; all imports are libc/libm/libgcc/zlib |\n| `ERRORS.md` | **710 rejection sites**: 368 diagnostics + 118 sentinel returns + 218 void returns + 6 FFI boundaries. Derived through the real C preprocessor, so `#if`-disabled dead code is excluded |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 20 axes → **154 rows** (colour type × depth × interlace × sizes × filters × zlib knobs × transforms × chunks × policies × limits × callbacks × formats) |\n| `ERROR_COVERAGE.md` | which rows the suite actually reached, per site |\n\n**Result of the final run** (`EXIT=0`):\n\n```\n12 test binaries, 136 tests: 135 passed, 0 failed, 1 ignored (by design)\nSYMBOLS.md        384/384, 0 missing\nCONFIGS.md        154/154 rows covered by a passing test\nERROR_COVERAGE.md 270/318 sites reached; 50 have no literal message; 48 unreached\n200,637 differential comparisons (machine-counted, not hand-counted)\n```\n\nThe 48 unreached sites are each listed with C reasoning: internal-consistency guards, checks needing >2 GiB objects, or checks *shadowed by an identical earlier test* in the same function.\n\n## Five real bugs found and fixed in the Rust\n\n1. **`png_sig_cmp`** returned `1` where C returned `115` — it returns `memcmp`'s value, whose *magnitude* is observable. Fixed by calling the C library's `memcmp`.\n2. **`png_chunk_warning(NULL, NULL)`** segfaulted; C prints `libpng warning: (null)` because `png_default_warning` passes the message straight to `fprintf`'s `%s`.\n3. **`png_set_cHRM`/`_XYZ`/`cLLI`/`mDCV`/`rgb_to_gray`** reported the *first* bad coordinate; gcc evaluates the `png_fixed()` argument list right-to-left, so C reports the *last*.\n4. **`png_write_chunk_start(png, NULL, 0)`** survived in Rust but segfaults in C — `PNG_CHUNK_FROM_STRING` dereferences in the argument list, and LLVM had sunk the loads past the callee's NULL guard. Fixed with `read_volatile`.\n5. **`png_image_write_to_memory` with `width == 0`** — C dies from `SIGFPE` (division by zero), Rust panicked into `SIGABRT`. Fixed with a `div`-instruction helper that raises the same hardware trap.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Nothing under `c_src/` was modified — all sources still carry their original timestamps.\n- Only one feature combination exists (`Cargo.toml` has no `[features]`); `tools/check_features.sh` derives that mechanically and runs `cargo check`, `cargo build --release` and the whole suite for it.\n- Calls that are fatal to the C library run in `fork()`ed children, so \"C segfaults here\" is a compared observation rather than the end of the run.\n- The suite was mutation-tested: a dozen single-token changes injected into the Rust library were each caught by the intended test, then reverted and the revert verified against the C.\n\n`VERIFICATION.md` documents the whole approach, including the known limits (libpng's `png_malloc`'d `big_row_buf` leaves padding bits uninitialised, so those bytes legitimately differ between two separate libraries and are excluded where relevant)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":900,"cache_read_input_tokens":559916,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":900,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"309de29f-cb7a-4138-9016-7ab2e7ef6079","uuid":"5c11a1db-4bec-4f2f-a89d-443a488eca9f","timestamp":"2026-08-23T05:43:52.934Z"}
